(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["C3"] = {"n":3,"level":"B1","t":"Unity, Coherence and Paragraph Types","lessons":[{"id":"3.1","t":"Unity and the Irrelevant Sentence","html":"<p><strong>Unit 3 · Lesson 3.1 · CEFR B1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Check that every sentence supports the topic sentence.</p>\n<p>2. Identify the irrelevant sentence in a paragraph.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يتحقق الطالب من أن كل جملة تدعم جملة الموضوع.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يحدد الجملة غير المرتبطة في الفقرة.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A paragraph has UNITY when every sentence supports the controlling idea of the topic sentence. At B1 level, irrelevant sentences are harder to see because they are usually about the same general subject. In a paragraph about the BENEFITS of learning a musical instrument, the sentence 'Some instruments, such as the piano, are very expensive' is about instruments, but it does not show a benefit, so it breaks the unity.</p>\n<p>There are four common kinds of irrelevant sentence in STEP: (1) a sentence on the same SUBJECT but not the same CONTROLLING IDEA (newspapers in general vs the benefits of reading newspapers); (2) a sentence that shares a KEY WORD but changes the topic (Red Sea coral in a paragraph about water resources); (3) a sentence that is TOO GENERAL (Technology has changed the world in many ways); and (4) a sentence that CONTRADICTS the topic (He often forgets his keys, in a paragraph about an organized person).</p>\n<p>To test each sentence, put it after the topic sentence and ask: Does this sentence prove or explain THIS controlling idea? Pay special attention to the controlling idea words: benefits, problems, ways, qualities, changes, improved. Remember that background sentences (Before the railway, the trip took forty days) can belong when they help explain the topic.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>topic</strong> Learning a musical instrument has many benefits for children. (controlling idea: benefits)</p>\n<p><strong>✓</strong> It improves their memory and concentration. (a benefit)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ same subject</strong> Some instruments, such as the piano, are very expensive. (about instruments, not benefits)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ key word</strong> The Red Sea has beautiful coral reefs. (in a paragraph about saving water)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ too general</strong> Technology has changed the world in many ways. (in a paragraph about phone addiction)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ contradiction</strong> He often forgets where he puts his keys. (in a paragraph about an organized person)</p>\n<p><strong>✓ background</strong> Before the railway, the trip took about forty days by camel. (explains why the railway mattered)</p>\n<p><strong>test</strong> Topic sentence + the sentence: does it prove THIS idea?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تتحقق وحدة الفقرة عندما تدعم كل جملة الفكرة المسيطرة في جملة الموضوع. وفي المستوى المتوسط تكون الجملة غير المرتبطة أصعب اكتشافًا لأنها عن الموضوع العام نفسه. وأنواعها: جملة عن الموضوع نفسه لكن ليس الفكرة المسيطرة، وجملة تشترك في كلمة مفتاحية وتغيّر الموضوع، وجملة عامة جدًا، وجملة تناقض الموضوع. واختبر كل جملة بوضعها بعد جملة الموضوع والسؤال: هل تثبت هذه الفكرة بالتحديد؟</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Underline the controlling idea in sentence 1 (benefits, ways, problems, qualities).</p>\n<p>2. Test each sentence against that controlling idea, not just the general subject.</p>\n<p>3. Be suspicious of sentences that repeat a key word but talk about something else.</p>\n<p>4. Look for sentences that contradict the topic or are much more general than the others.</p>\n<p>5. Keep background sentences that help explain the topic.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ضع خطًا تحت الفكرة المسيطرة في الجملة الأولى، واختبر كل جملة مقابل هذه الفكرة لا الموضوع العام فقط، واحذر من الجمل التي تكرر كلمة مفتاحية وتتحدث عن شيء آخر، ومن الجمل المتناقضة أو العامة جدًا، واحتفظ بالجمل التي تقدم خلفية مفيدة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ Choosing a background sentence that actually helps explain the topic.</p>\n<p>✗ Missing a sentence that repeats a key word but changes the topic.</p>\n<p>✗ Choosing the concluding sentence because it sounds general.</p>\n<p>✗ Missing a sentence that contradicts the topic sentence.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Social media has changed the way people get news. <strong>(2)</strong> Many people now read news on their phones instead of in newspapers. <strong>(3)</strong> News spreads within minutes. <strong>(4)</strong> My favourite app is a photo-editing app. <strong>(5)</strong> However, some news on social media is false. <strong>(6)</strong> Readers must check their sources carefully.</p>\n<p>A. Sentence 3 B. Sentence 4 C. Sentence 5 D. Sentence 6</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Controlling idea: how people get news has changed.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentences 2, 3, 5 and 6 are all about news on social media.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 4 is about the writer's favourite app, not about news.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الرابعة عن الموضوع العام لكنها ليست عن الأخبار.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Water is one of Saudi Arabia's most valuable resources. <strong>(2)</strong> The country has very little rainfall. <strong>(3)</strong> Most of its drinking water comes from desalination plants. <strong>(4)</strong> These plants remove salt from seawater. <strong>(5)</strong> The Red Sea has beautiful coral reefs. <strong>(6)</strong> Saving water at home is therefore very important. <strong>(7)</strong> Small actions, like fixing leaking taps, make a big difference.</p>\n<p>A. Sentence 2 B. Sentence 3 C. Sentence 4 D. Sentence 5</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Controlling idea: water is a valuable resource.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 4 mentions seawater, and sentence 5 mentions the Red Sea: a key-word trap.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Coral reefs do not support the idea of water as a resource, so sentence 5 is irrelevant.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">احذر من الكلمات المشتركة؛ الجملة الخامسة تغيّر الموضوع.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>My grandfather grew up without electricity. In the evenings, his family used oil lamps. ______ He says that life was harder, but people spent more time together.</p>\n<p>A. Instead of watching television, they told stories and sang songs.</p>\n<p>B. Electricity was discovered long ago.</p>\n<p>C. Oil is Saudi Arabia's main export.</p>\n<p>D. My grandfather is now eighty years old.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Topic: life without electricity in the grandfather's childhood.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The next sentence says people spent more time together.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'they told stories and sang songs' supports that idea.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اختر الجملة التي تحافظ على وحدة الفقرة وتربط ما قبلها بما بعدها.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B1-01 — The benefits of learning a second language</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a paragraph of 100–150 words about the benefits of learning a second language. Make sure every sentence supports your controlling idea (benefits).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب فقرة من مئة إلى مئة وخمسين كلمة عن فوائد تعلم لغة ثانية، وتأكد من أن كل جملة تدعم الفكرة المسيطرة (الفوائد).</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence with a clear controlling idea (benefits).</p>\n<p>2. Benefit 1 + explanation or example (jobs).</p>\n<p>3. Benefit 2 + explanation (culture).</p>\n<p>4. Benefit 3 + evidence (the brain).</p>\n<p>5. Benefit 4 (travel).</p>\n<p>6. Concluding sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (112 words; target 100–150)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Learning a second language brings many benefits. First, it opens doors to better jobs. Many companies in Saudi Arabia, especially in tourism, banking and technology, need employees who can communicate in English. Second, it helps us understand other cultures. When we read books or watch films in another language, we learn how other people think and live. Third, studies show that learning a language improves memory and problem-solving skills, because the brain has to switch between two systems. Finally, it makes travel easier and more enjoyable, since we can talk to local people instead of depending on translation apps. For all these reasons, every student should take learning a second language seriously.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The controlling idea (benefits) is clear in the topic sentence.</p>\n<p>▸ Each supporting sentence gives one benefit and explains it with an example or a reason.</p>\n<p>▸ There are no off-topic sentences: nothing about the difficulty of grammar or the writer's teacher.</p>\n<p>▸ First, Second, Third and Finally organize the benefits, and the conclusion restates the main idea.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my topic sentence have a clear controlling idea?</p>\n<p>☐ Does EVERY sentence support that controlling idea?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I remove sentences that are only about the general subject?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I explain each point with an example or a reason?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 100–150 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ كل جملة واسأل: هل تدعم فكرة الفوائد تحديدًا؟ احذف أي جملة عن الموضوع العام لا تدعم الفكرة المسيطرة.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 A","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Learning to play a musical instrument has many benefits for children. (2) It improves their memory and concentration. (3) Some instruments, such as the piano, are very expensive. (4) It also teaches them patience, because progress takes time. (5) Playing in a group helps them work with others. (6) For these reasons, many schools offer music lessons."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The price of instruments is not a benefit.","h":"سعر الآلات ليس فائدة."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Public transport has several advantages for big cities. (2) It reduces traffic because one bus can carry many people. (3) It also reduces air pollution. (4) In addition, it is cheaper than owning a car. (5) Many people enjoy driving their own cars at the weekend. (6) Therefore, cities should invest more in buses and trains."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Enjoying driving is not an advantage of public transport.","h":"متعة القيادة ليست ميزة للنقل العام."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) The Kingdom Centre is one of the most famous buildings in Riyadh. (2) Riyadh's summers are extremely hot and dry. (3) It is 302 metres tall. (4) It has an unusual shape with a large opening at the top. (5) Inside, there is a shopping mall, a hotel and offices. (6) Visitors can walk across a bridge at the top. (7) At night, it is lit up in different colours."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — Riyadh's weather is about the city, not the building.","h":"طقس الرياض لا يصف المبنى."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Reading newspapers is a good habit for students. (2) It keeps them informed about events in the world. (3) It improves their vocabulary and reading speed. (4) Some newspapers are printed in more than one language. (5) It also gives them ideas for essays and discussions. (6) Students should read a newspaper at least once a week."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — It is about newspapers, but it does not show why reading them is a good habit.","h":"عن الصحف لكنه ليس فائدة للقراءة."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Our school canteen has improved a lot this year. (2) It now sells fresh salads and fruit. (3) Fried food has been replaced with grilled food. (4) The prices are still low. (5) The queues are shorter because there are two new counters. (6) Many students bring lunch from home. (7) Most students agree that the canteen is now much better."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — Bringing lunch from home does not show how the canteen improved.","h":"إحضار الغداء لا يبين تحسن المقصف."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Volunteering at a hospital taught my brother many things. (2) Hospitals in big cities are often very crowded. (3) He learned how to talk to patients kindly. (4) He saw how hard doctors and nurses work. (5) He also learned to stay calm in difficult situations. (6) Now he wants to study medicine."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — Crowded hospitals are not something the brother learned.","h":"ازدحام المستشفيات ليس مما تعلمه الأخ."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) The date palm is very important in Saudi culture. (2) Its fruit has been a main food for centuries. (3) Its leaves were used to make baskets and roofs. (4) Coconut palms grow mainly in tropical countries. (5) Its wood was used for building. (6) Even today, it appears on the national emblem. (7) No other tree is as valued in Arabia."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Coconut palms share the word palm but are a different topic.","h":"نخيل جوز الهند يشترك في الكلمة فقط."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Sleeping well before an exam is very important. (2) Sleep helps the brain store information. (3) Tired students make more careless mistakes. (4) They also find it harder to concentrate. (5) A good night's sleep improves mood and confidence. (6) Some students prefer to study in groups."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — Studying in groups is not about sleep before exams.","h":"الدراسة الجماعية خارج موضوع النوم."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Desert plants have special ways to survive. (2) Many have long roots that reach water deep underground. (3) Desert animals usually sleep during the day. (4) Some store water in their thick stems. (5) Others have small leaves that lose less water. (6) Some seeds wait for years until it rains. (7) These features allow plants to live where others cannot."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The paragraph is about plants; animals are a different topic.","h":"الحيوانات خارج موضوع النباتات."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) My cousin Faisal is a very organized person. (2) He plans his week every Sunday evening. (3) He keeps his notes in labelled folders. (4) He often forgets where he puts his keys. (5) He always arrives on time. (6) His teachers often ask him to help other students plan their work."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Forgetting his keys contradicts the idea that he is organized.","h":"نسيان المفاتيح يناقض فكرة التنظيم."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) The Hejaz Railway was built in the early twentieth century. (2) It connected Damascus with Madinah. (3) It made the pilgrimage journey much shorter and safer. (4) Before the railway, the trip took about forty days by camel. (5) Modern high-speed trains in Japan can travel at over 300 kilometres an hour. (6) The railway was damaged during the First World War. (7) Today, its old station in Madinah is a museum."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Japanese trains are about railways in general, not the Hejaz Railway.","h":"قطارات اليابان خارج موضوع سكة الحجاز."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) There are several ways to reduce stress during exams. (2) First, make a realistic study timetable. (3) Exams usually take place at the end of each term. (4) Second, take short breaks every hour. (5) Third, eat healthy food and drink plenty of water. (6) Finally, sleep at least eight hours a night."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — When exams happen is not a way to reduce stress.","h":"موعد الاختبارات ليس طريقة لتقليل التوتر."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) My first day at secondary school was memorable. (2) I woke up early because I was excited. (3) The building was much bigger than my old school. (4) I got lost twice looking for my classroom. (5) Luckily, an older student showed me the way. (6) By the end of the day, I had made three new friends. (7) Secondary school lasts for three years in Saudi Arabia."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 7 — A general fact about secondary school is not part of the story of the first day.","h":"حقيقة عامة لا تنتمي إلى قصة اليوم الأول."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Electric cars are becoming more popular. (2) They do not produce exhaust fumes. (3) They are quiet and cheap to run. (4) Charging stations are being built in many cities. (5) Petrol was first used in cars more than a hundred years ago. (6) Many experts believe most new cars will be electric by 2040."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — The history of petrol does not explain the popularity of electric cars.","h":"تاريخ البنزين لا يفسر انتشار السيارات الكهربائية."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Good teachers share some important qualities. (2) Teaching is one of the oldest professions in the world. (3) They explain ideas clearly and patiently. (4) They know each student's strengths and weaknesses. (5) They encourage students to ask questions. (6) They also show respect to everyone in the class. (7) Students remember such teachers for the rest of their lives."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — The history of teaching is not a quality of good teachers.","h":"تاريخ التعليم ليس صفة للمعلم الجيد."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Smartphone addiction is a growing problem among teenagers. (2) Many teenagers check their phones more than a hundred times a day. (3) Some feel anxious when they are away from their phones. (4) Technology has changed the world in many ways. (5) Others lose sleep because they use their phones late at night. (6) Parents and schools need to help teenagers use phones more wisely."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — This sentence is too general; it does not show the problem of addiction.","h":"جملة عامة جدًا لا تبين مشكلة الإدمان."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Bees are essential for our food supply. (2) They pollinate many fruits and vegetables. (3) Without them, farmers would produce much less food. (4) Bee numbers are falling in many parts of the world. (5) Pesticides and loss of habitat are the main causes. (6) Wasps can be dangerous if they sting. (7) Protecting bees means protecting our food."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — Wasps are a different insect and do not support the topic.","h":"الدبابير خارج موضوع النحل."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) The Corniche in Jeddah attracts thousands of visitors. (2) Jeddah's airport is one of the busiest in the country. (3) People come to walk, cycle and enjoy the sea breeze. (4) There are parks, playgrounds and sculptures along the way. (5) The King Fahd Fountain is one of the highest in the world. (6) In the evening, families have picnics by the water."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — The airport is in Jeddah but is not part of the Corniche.","h":"المطار في جدة لكنه ليس من الكورنيش."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Saudi food is famous for its rich flavours.","By the time the family sits down together, it is often after ten o'clock.","Some children prefer to eat fast food.","Many restaurants in Riyadh are open all night."],"x":["Many families in Saudi Arabia now eat dinner very late. Parents often finish work in the evening, and children have activities after school. ______ As a result, children may not get enough sleep before school."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] By the time the family sits down together, it is often after ten o'clock. — The gap links the busy schedule to the late dinner and the lack of sleep.","h":"الجملة تربط الانشغال بالعشاء المتأخر وقلة النوم."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Football is the most popular sport in the world.","The school also has a basketball court.","A new coach has also taught them better teamwork.","Some students prefer swimming to football."],"x":["Our school's football team has improved greatly this year. The players train four times a week instead of two. ______ As a result, they won the regional cup for the first time."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] A new coach has also taught them better teamwork. — The gap needs another reason for the team's improvement.","h":"سبب آخر لتحسن الفريق."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Diagrams are useful in science.","Students learn in different ways.","Teachers should speak clearly.","Hands-on activities can be noisy."],"x":["______ Some students learn best by listening to explanations. Others need to see pictures and diagrams. Many learn by doing activities with their hands."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Students learn in different ways. — The details are different learning styles.","h":"التفاصيل أساليب تعلم مختلفة."},{"n":22,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) However, when he looked out of the window, he saw it was raining heavily.","(2) Majed had planned a picnic with his friends.","(3) So they decided to watch a film at his house instead.","(4) He woke up early to prepare the food."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — plan → preparation → However, rain → So, a new plan.","h":"خطة ثم تحضير ثم مشكلة ثم حل."},{"n":23,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","However","For example","In addition"],"x":["The new road was supposed to reduce traffic. ______, the traffic has become even worse."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] However — The result is the opposite of what was expected: contrast.","h":"النتيجة عكس المتوقع."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Cafés are very popular in Riyadh.","Apps are used by millions of people.","Clearly, a new generation of entrepreneurs is growing in Saudi Arabia.","Loans must be paid back."],"x":["Many young Saudis are starting their own businesses. Some open cafés and restaurants. Others create apps or sell products online. The government also offers loans and training to help them. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Clearly, a new generation of entrepreneurs is growing in Saudi Arabia. — The conclusion sums up all the evidence.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص الأدلة."},{"n":25,"s":"Each of the players (A) have (B) their own (C) locker in (D) the changing room.","o":["have","their","locker","the"],"k":0,"e":"[error] have — Each is singular: has.","h":"Each مفرد فنستخدم has."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Banks offer different types of accounts.","Money was invented thousands of years ago.","Some teenagers have part-time jobs abroad.","They often want to buy the latest phones, clothes and games."],"x":["Saving money is not always easy for teenagers. ______ One solution is to save a small part of any money they receive."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They often want to buy the latest phones, clothes and games. — The gap explains why saving is difficult before the solution.","h":"الجملة تشرح الصعوبة قبل الحل."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence is the most appropriate for a formal school report?","o":["The majority of students preferred online lessons.","Loads of students liked online lessons.","Most guys were into online lessons.","Online lessons were, like, popular."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] The majority of students preferred online lessons. — A report needs formal words: the majority of, preferred.","h":"التقرير يحتاج كلمات رسمية."},{"n":28,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["Because the bridge was closed. We had to take a longer route.","The bridge was closed, we had to take a longer route.","Because the bridge was closed, we had to take a longer route.","Because the bridge was closed, so we had to take a longer route."],"k":2,"e":"[error] Because the bridge was closed, we had to take a longer route. — because-part + comma + main idea, without so.","h":"because دون so."},{"n":29,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["as a result","for example","in addition","on the other hand"],"x":["Riyadh is very hot in summer. Abha, ______, is cool and rainy."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] on the other hand — Two cities with opposite weather: contrast.","h":"مدينتان بطقس متعاكس."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Photography has changed a lot over the past twenty years. (2) Most people now take photos with their phones instead of cameras. (3) My uncle's favourite hobby is fishing. (4) Photos can be shared instantly online. (5) Editing apps allow anyone to improve their pictures."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The uncle's fishing is off the topic of changes in photography.","h":"هواية الصيد خارج الموضوع."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"3.2","t":"Coherence and Logical Order","html":"<p><strong>Unit 3 · Lesson 3.2 · CEFR B1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Arrange sentences in logical order (time, space, importance).</p>\n<p>2. Choose the best order for a set of sentences.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يرتب الطالب الجمل ترتيبًا منطقيًا (زمنيًا ومكانيًا وحسب الأهمية).</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار أفضل ترتيب لمجموعة من الجمل.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A paragraph is COHERENT when its sentences follow a logical order and connect smoothly. Writers use different kinds of order: TIME order for stories and processes (first, then, two years later); SPACE order for descriptions (in front of, behind, beyond); IMPORTANCE order for reasons and arguments (first of all … most importantly); GENERAL → SPECIFIC (a general statement, then examples); and CAUSE → EFFECT or PROBLEM → SOLUTION.</p>\n<p>Coherence also depends on links between sentences. Pronouns and determiners (he, it, this, these, such) must come AFTER the noun they refer to. Transition words show the relationship: however (contrast), as a result / because of this (effect), for example (example), similarly (comparison), to solve this problem (solution). A sentence that starts with However or As a result can never be the first sentence.</p>\n<p>For STEP best-order items: (1) find the sentence that introduces the topic and contains no reference words; (2) look for clear pairs, such as a problem and 'To solve this problem …', or a noun and the next sentence with 'it'; (3) find the sentence that ends the paragraph (Today …, Finally …, Therefore …); (4) check the options that match your pairs and read the best one from start to finish.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>time</strong> My uncle started cooking at twelve. → After finishing school, he trained as a chef. → Two years later, he opened a restaurant. → Today, it is very popular.</p>\n<p><strong>space</strong> The house is at the end of a quiet street. → In front of it, there are palm trees. → Behind it, there is a garden. → Beyond the garden, you can see the mountains.</p>\n<p><strong>importance</strong> First of all, … → It also … → Most importantly, …</p>\n<p><strong>problem → solution</strong> Riyadh had heavy traffic. → People spent hours in their cars. → To solve this problem, the city built a metro. → Now, thousands travel by metro.</p>\n<p><strong>pronoun</strong> My sister travelled to Spain. → She had studied Spanish for three years. (She after My sister)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ first</strong> However, it can be dangerous … (However cannot open a paragraph)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ first</strong> This made prices rise. (This needs something before it)</p>\n<p><strong>pair</strong> To apply, first read the conditions. → Next, collect your certificates.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تكون الفقرة مترابطة عندما تتبع جملها ترتيبًا منطقيًا وتتصل بسلاسة: ترتيب زمني للقصص والخطوات، ومكاني للوصف، وحسب الأهمية للأسباب والحجج، ومن العام إلى الخاص، ومن السبب إلى النتيجة أو من المشكلة إلى الحل. ويجب أن تأتي الضمائر وكلمات الإشارة مثل it وthis بعد الاسم الذي تعود إليه، ولا يمكن أن تبدأ الفقرة بجملة فيها However أو As a result.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the opening sentence: it introduces the topic and has no he / it / this / however / as a result.</p>\n<p>2. Find pairs that must stay together: a noun and its pronoun, a problem and its solution, a cause and its result.</p>\n<p>3. Find the closing sentence: Today …, Finally …, Therefore …, Most importantly …</p>\n<p>4. Eliminate options that break a pair or start with the wrong sentence.</p>\n<p>5. Read the chosen order from start to finish to check that it flows.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الجملة الافتتاحية التي تقدم الموضوع بلا ضمائر أو أدوات ربط، ثم عن الأزواج التي يجب أن تبقى معًا كالاسم وضميره والمشكلة وحلها، ثم عن الجملة الختامية، واستبعد البدائل التي تكسر الأزواج، ثم اقرأ الترتيب كاملًا.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ An order that starts with a sentence containing However, This or As a result.</p>\n<p>✗ A pronoun placed before the noun it refers to.</p>\n<p>✗ A solution placed before the problem it solves.</p>\n<p>✗ Most importantly placed before the less important points.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Choose the best order for the sentences.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> Then she moved to London to study architecture.</p>\n<p><strong>(2)</strong> Zaha Hadid was born in Baghdad in 1950.</p>\n<p><strong>(3)</strong> Later, she designed famous buildings around the world.</p>\n<p><strong>(4)</strong> As a child, she was interested in design and art.</p>\n<p>A. 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 B. 4 – 2 – 1 – 3 C. 2 – 4 – 3 – 1 D. 2 – 4 – 1 – 3</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 2 names the person and gives the start of her life: it opens the paragraph.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Childhood (4) comes before studying (1), and 'Later' (3) comes last.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The order is 2 – 4 – 1 – 3.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابدأ بالجملة التي تذكر الاسم والولادة، ثم اتبع الترتيب الزمني.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Choose the best order for the sentences.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>(1)</strong> The most important reason, however, is that it keeps families connected.</p>\n<p><strong>(2)</strong> Video calls have many advantages.</p>\n<p><strong>(3)</strong> First, they are free or very cheap.</p>\n<p><strong>(4)</strong> Second, they are easy to use.</p>\n<p>A. 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 B. 2 – 1 – 3 – 4 C. 3 – 2 – 4 – 1 D. 2 – 3 – 1 – 4</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Sentence 2 introduces the topic: advantages of video calls.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> First and Second come next in order.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'The most important reason' comes last for emphasis: 2 – 3 – 4 – 1.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">السبب الأهم يأتي في النهاية للتأكيد.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The festival was a great success. ______ Even the weather was perfect. Everyone wants it to happen again next year.</p>\n<p>A. Festivals are common in many countries.</p>\n<p>B. Next year, the festival will be in June.</p>\n<p>C. More than ten thousand people attended, and the food stalls were busy all day.</p>\n<p>D. The weather forecast is not always correct.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The topic sentence says the festival was a success.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'Even the weather was perfect' adds one more positive point, so the gap needs other evidence of success.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only the sentence about ten thousand people and busy food stalls fits.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">Even تعني إضافة دليل آخر، فالفراغ يحتاج دليلًا أول.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B1-02 — A memorable family Eid celebration</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write 100–150 words about a memorable family Eid celebration. Use clear time order and time expressions so the reader can follow the day from morning to night.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب من مئة إلى مئة وخمسين كلمة عن احتفال عيد لا يُنسى مع أسرتك، واستخدم ترتيبًا زمنيًا واضحًا وعبارات زمنية ليتابع القارئ اليوم من الصباح إلى الليل.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: which Eid, and why it was memorable.</p>\n<p>2. Early morning: prayer, new clothes.</p>\n<p>3. Late morning: visiting relatives, food.</p>\n<p>4. Afternoon: an activity or a special moment.</p>\n<p>5. Night: how the day ended.</p>\n<p>6. Concluding sentence: what the day taught you.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (124 words; target 100–150)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Last Eid al-Fitr was the most memorable Eid for my family. Early in the morning, we put on our new clothes and went to the Eid prayer at the large mosque near our house. After the prayer, we visited my grandparents in Taif, where all my uncles, aunts and cousins had gathered. My grandmother had prepared a huge breakfast with dates, Arabic coffee and fresh bread. Then the children received their Eidiyah, and my youngest cousin was so excited that he counted his money three times. In the afternoon, we went to a park, where there were fireworks and traditional dances. Finally, late at night, we drove home tired but happy. That day reminded me how important it is to spend time with family.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ Time expressions (Early in the morning, After the prayer, In the afternoon, Finally) create clear coherence.</p>\n<p>▸ Pronouns (we, he, she) always follow the nouns they refer to.</p>\n<p>▸ A specific, funny detail (counting money three times) makes the paragraph memorable.</p>\n<p>▸ The concluding sentence moves from the events to a reflection.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Do my events follow a clear time order?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use at least four time expressions?</p>\n<p>☐ Does every pronoun clearly refer to a noun before it?</p>\n<p>☐ Does my concluding sentence reflect on the day?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 100–150 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من الترتيب الزمني ومن العبارات الزمنية، ومن أن كل ضمير يعود إلى اسم قبله، ومن أن الخاتمة تأمل في اليوم.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 D · Example 2 A · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) It was built in 1930 by the city's first mayor.","(2) Our city has a famous old clock tower.","(3) Today, it is the symbol of our city.","(4) The tower stands in the main square and can be seen from far away."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — general → location → history → Today.","h":"من العام إلى الخاص ثم اليوم."},{"n":2,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","4 – 2 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) Most importantly, it keeps your heart healthy.","(2) Swimming is an excellent form of exercise.","(3) It also improves your breathing.","(4) First of all, it uses almost every muscle in the body."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 3 – 1 — topic → First of all → also → Most importantly.","h":"ترتيب حسب الأهمية."},{"n":3,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 1 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) Behind the house, there is a small vegetable garden.","(2) My grandparents' house is at the end of a quiet street.","(3) In front of the house, there are two tall palm trees.","(4) Beyond the garden, you can see the mountains."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — the house → in front → behind → beyond the garden.","h":"ترتيب مكاني."},{"n":4,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) As a result, he missed the bus.","(2) Hamad's alarm didn't ring this morning.","(3) He woke up forty minutes late.","(4) Because of this, he arrived late for his first exam."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — cause → effect → result → final result.","h":"سلسلة سبب ونتيجة."},{"n":5,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 4 – 1 – 2","1 – 3 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 2 – 4","3 – 1 – 4 – 2"],"x":["(1) Many people spent two hours a day in their cars.","(2) Now, thousands of people travel by metro every day.","(3) Riyadh used to have very heavy traffic.","(4) To solve this problem, the city built a new metro system."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 4 – 2 — problem → detail → solution → result now.","h":"مشكلة ثم حل ثم نتيجة."},{"n":6,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 5 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 1 – 5 – 3 – 4","5 – 2 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 5 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) When she opened it, she found a gold necklace.","(2) Last Eid, my sister received a small box from our aunt.","(3) She was so happy that she cried.","(4) She thanked our aunt and wore it immediately.","(5) It was wrapped in beautiful red paper."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 5 – 1 – 3 – 4 — the box → the wrapping → opening it → her feeling → her action.","h":"رتّب أحداث الهدية."},{"n":7,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) Once the form is complete, submit it before the deadline.","(2) To apply for the scholarship, first read the conditions carefully.","(3) Next, collect your certificates and a copy of your ID.","(4) Then fill in the online form."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — first → Next → Then → Once complete.","h":"خطوات التقديم."},{"n":8,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) However, it can also be dangerous if people do not follow safety rules.","(2) Swimming in the sea is a popular summer activity.","(3) For example, some swimmers go too far from the beach.","(4) It is fun and good for health."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — topic → positive → However, danger → For example.","h":"إيجابي ثم However ثم مثال على الخطر."},{"n":9,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 1 – 4 – 2","3 – 4 – 1 – 2","1 – 3 – 4 – 2","3 – 1 – 2 – 4"],"x":["(1) Riyadh, for example, has modern buildings and museums.","(2) Finally, AlUla offers amazing ancient sites in the desert.","(3) Saudi Arabia has many attractive cities for tourists.","(4) Similarly, Jeddah is famous for its old houses and sea views."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 3 – 1 – 4 – 2 — general → for example → Similarly → Finally.","h":"عام ثم أمثلة."},{"n":10,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 5 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 5 – 3","2 – 4 – 5 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) The water vapour rises and cools in the sky.","(2) The sun heats water in seas and rivers.","(3) Finally, the water falls back to the earth as rain.","(4) It turns into water vapour.","(5) As it cools, it forms clouds."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3 — heat → vapour → rises and cools → clouds → rain.","h":"دورة الماء بالترتيب."},{"n":11,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["4 – 3 – 1 – 2","1 – 4 – 3 – 2","4 – 1 – 2 – 3","4 – 1 – 3 – 2"],"x":["(1) After finishing school, he trained as a chef in Jeddah.","(2) Today, his restaurant is one of the most popular in Taif.","(3) Two years later, he opened his own small restaurant.","(4) My uncle started cooking when he was only twelve."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 4 – 1 – 3 – 2 — childhood → training → two years later → today.","h":"ترتيب زمني."},{"n":12,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) Second, they can learn from their mistakes without fear.","(2) Online lessons have some advantages for shy students.","(3) First, they can ask questions by typing instead of speaking.","(4) Therefore, teachers should consider using online tools for some activities."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 — topic → First → Second → Therefore.","h":"موضوع ثم أولًا ثم ثانيًا ثم النتيجة."},{"n":13,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 5 – 3 – 4","2 – 5 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 5 – 1 – 3 – 4","5 – 2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) Without enough water from the wells, farmers could not grow their crops.","(2) Last year, there was very little rain in our region.","(3) As a result, the price of vegetables went up.","(4) Many families had to spend more money on food.","(5) The wells also began to dry up."],"k":2,"e":"[best order] 2 – 5 – 1 – 3 – 4 — little rain → wells dry → no crops → prices up → families spend more.","h":"سلسلة أسباب ونتائج."},{"n":14,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 4 – 2 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","3 – 2 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) This helped her talk to people everywhere she went.","(2) She was surprised how much Spanish she could understand.","(3) My sister Maha travelled to Spain last summer.","(4) She had studied it for three years before the trip."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 3 – 2 – 4 – 1 — Maha → understood Spanish → had studied it → This helped her.","h":"الاسم قبل الضمائر."},{"n":15,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["3 – 2 – 4 – 1 – 5","3 – 4 – 2 – 1 – 5","2 – 3 – 4 – 1 – 5","3 – 2 – 1 – 4 – 5"],"x":["(1) I would be grateful if you could reply by Thursday.","(2) I am writing to ask whether our class could visit your factory.","(3) Dear Mr. Nasser,","(4) We are studying how food is produced, and a visit would help us greatly.","(5) Yours sincerely, Ms. Hind"],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 3 – 2 – 4 – 1 – 5 — greeting → purpose → reason → request for reply → closing.","h":"ترتيب الرسالة الرسمية."},{"n":16,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 4","1 – 2 – 3 – 4","2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) For instance, students can choose subjects they really enjoy.","(2) In my opinion, students should have more choice at school.","(3) This would make them more motivated.","(4) As a result, their grades would probably improve."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 3 – 4 — opinion → example → This → As a result.","h":"رأي ثم مثال ثم نتيجة."},{"n":17,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["First of all","Most importantly","For example","In contrast"],"x":["Exercise helps you sleep better and improves your mood. ______, it reduces the risk of serious diseases."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] Most importantly — The strongest point comes last: Most importantly.","h":"النقطة الأقوى في النهاية."},{"n":18,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Similarly","For instance","Meanwhile","Consequently"],"x":["The weather was terrible. ______, the match was cancelled."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Consequently — The cancellation is the result of the weather.","h":"الإلغاء نتيجة للطقس."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Then they sold the bottles to a recycling company.","Plastic takes hundreds of years to break down.","The school library has five thousand books.","Some students did not want to help."],"x":["First, the students collected plastic bottles from around the school. ______ Finally, they used the money to buy new books for the library."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Then they sold the bottles to a recycling company. — 'the money' needs a step that produces money.","h":"the money تحتاج خطوة تجلب المال."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The new country was very cold in winter.","My family moved because of my father's job.","Slowly, however, I learned the language and made some good friends.","Learning a language takes many years."],"x":["At first, I found living in a new country very difficult. I didn't understand the language, and I had no friends. ______ Now I feel completely at home."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Slowly, however, I learned the language and made some good friends. — The gap explains the change from difficult to at home.","h":"الجملة تشرح التغير."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Coffee shops have become very popular in Saudi cities. (2) Young people meet there to talk and study. (3) Many have free internet and comfortable seats. (4) Some even hold book clubs and art events. (5) Coffee beans are grown in many tropical countries. (6) For many, the coffee shop has become a second home."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Where coffee beans grow does not explain the popularity of coffee shops.","h":"مكان زراعة البن لا يفسر انتشار المقاهي."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["The deep sea is very dark.","Rivers are full of life.","Fish are extremely varied.","Coins are made of metal."],"x":["______ Some are as small as a coin, while others are bigger than a person. Some live in the deep sea, and others live in rivers. They come in almost every colour."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Fish are extremely varied. — The details show variety in size, home and colour.","h":"التفاصيل تبين التنوع."},{"n":23,"s":"When I (A) arrived at the party, most of the guests (B) have already (C) left, so I (D) felt disappointed.","o":["arrived","have already","left","felt"],"k":1,"e":"[error] have already — The leaving happened before the arrival in the past: had already left.","h":"الماضي التام had already."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Exams are usually held in the morning.","Some students study in the library.","Therefore, taking regular breaks is a smarter way to study.","Research is done in many universities."],"x":["Many students believe that studying for long hours without a break is the best way to prepare for exams. However, research shows that the brain works better with short, regular breaks. Students who take a ten-minute break every hour remember more. They also feel less tired. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] Therefore, taking regular breaks is a smarter way to study. — The conclusion states what the evidence shows.","h":"الخاتمة تذكر ما يثبته الدليل."},{"n":25,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","For example","However","As a result"],"x":["My brother is very good at maths. ______, he is not very interested in science."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] However — good at maths / not interested in science: an unexpected contrast.","h":"تضاد غير متوقع."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is the most appropriate in a formal letter of complaint?","o":["Your service was rubbish!","I am writing to complain about the poor service I received.","I'm super angry about your service.","You guys did a bad job."],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] I am writing to complain about the poor service I received. — A formal complaint uses polite, formal language.","h":"الشكوى الرسمية بلغة رسمية مهذبة."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["In fact, the hump stores fat, not water.","Camels can walk for long distances.","Water is very important in the desert.","Some camels have two humps."],"x":["Many people think that camels can store water in their humps. ______ The fat gives them energy when food is not available."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] In fact, the hump stores fat, not water. — The gap corrects the belief and introduces 'The fat'.","h":"الجملة تصحح الاعتقاد وتمهد لكلمة الدهون."},{"n":28,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["My friend who is a talented artist. Painted this picture.","My friend is a talented artist, painted this picture.","My friend, who is a talented artist, painted this picture.","My friend, who is a talented artist painted, this picture."],"k":2,"e":"[error] My friend, who is a talented artist, painted this picture. — The who-part is between commas inside a complete sentence.","h":"عبارة who بين فاصلتين داخل جملة كاملة."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","4 – 2 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) In the end, they reached a good agreement.","(2) The two companies disagreed about the price.","(3) Then they met several times to discuss it.","(4) At first, neither side wanted to change its offer."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 3 – 1 — problem → At first → Then → In the end.","h":"مشكلة ثم مراحل الحل."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Recycling paper saves trees. (2) It also uses less water and energy than making new paper. (3) Paper was first invented in China. (4) Recycled paper can be used for newspapers and boxes. (5) Many schools now collect used paper. (6) Students can help by putting paper in the right bins. (7) Every sheet we recycle makes a difference."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — The history of paper is not about recycling.","h":"تاريخ الورق ليس عن إعادة التدوير."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"3.3","t":"Transitions in Context (Addition, Contrast, Result, Example)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 3 · Lesson 3.3 · CEFR B1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Choose transitions for addition, contrast, result and example.</p>\n<p>2. Punctuate transitions correctly.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يختار الطالب أدوات الانتقال المناسبة للإضافة والتضاد والنتيجة والمثال.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يرقّم أدوات الانتقال ترقيمًا صحيحًا.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>Transitions show the RELATIONSHIP between ideas. ADDITION: in addition, moreover, furthermore, also. CONTRAST: however, on the other hand, nevertheless, even so, in fact (to correct a belief), whereas, although, despite. RESULT: therefore, as a result, consequently, so, in this way. EXAMPLE: for example, for instance, such as. CONDITION: otherwise (= if not).</p>\n<p>Grammar matters as much as meaning. However, therefore, moreover, nevertheless and consequently join two SENTENCES: It was hot. However, we went out. / It was hot; however, we went out. They are followed by a comma. Although, whereas and because join two CLAUSES inside one sentence: Although it was hot, we went out. Despite and in spite of are followed by a NOUN or -ing form, not a clause: Despite the heat, … (not Despite it was hot, and never despite of). Although and but are never used together.</p>\n<p>To answer a STEP transition item, cover the options and decide the relationship between the two ideas: Is the second idea similar (addition), opposite or surprising (contrast), a consequence (result), or a specific case (example)? Then choose the transition from that group that also fits the grammar and punctuation of the sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>addition</strong> Fruit contains vitamins. In addition, it is rich in fibre.</p>\n<p><strong>contrast</strong> The phone is expensive. Nevertheless, many people are buying it.</p>\n<p><strong>contrast</strong> My brother likes the city, whereas my sister prefers the countryside.</p>\n<p><strong>result</strong> Ahmed did not revise. Therefore, he got a low mark.</p>\n<p><strong>example</strong> Some animals hunt at night. Owls, for example, hunt in the dark.</p>\n<p><strong>despite</strong> Despite the heat, thousands of fans watched the match.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> Although it rained, but we played. → Although it rained, we played.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ → ✓</strong> It was hot, however we went out. → It was hot; however, we went out.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تبين أدوات الانتقال العلاقة بين الأفكار: الإضافة (in addition, moreover, furthermore)، والتضاد (however, on the other hand, nevertheless, whereas, although, despite)، والنتيجة (therefore, as a result, consequently)، والمثال (for example, such as)، والشرط (otherwise). وتربط however وtherefore بين جملتين ويليها فاصلة، أما although وwhereas فتربطان داخل الجملة الواحدة، ويأتي بعد despite اسم أو فعل بـ ing، ولا تجتمع although مع but.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Cover the options and decide the relationship: addition, contrast, result, example or condition.</p>\n<p>2. Choose the group of transitions that matches that relationship.</p>\n<p>3. Check the grammar: a full sentence after however / therefore; a clause after although / whereas; a noun after despite / such as.</p>\n<p>4. Check punctuation: a comma after a sentence-joining transition, a semicolon or full stop before it.</p>\n<p>5. Read the full sentence with your choice to make sure it makes sense.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">غطِّ البدائل وحدد العلاقة بين الفكرتين، ثم اختر من مجموعة الأدوات المناسبة، وتحقق من القواعد (جملة بعد however، وجملة فرعية بعد although، واسم بعد despite) ومن الترقيم، ثم اقرأ الجملة كاملة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A result transition where the ideas are in contrast.</p>\n<p>✗ although + but in one sentence.</p>\n<p>✗ despite + a full clause, or despite of.</p>\n<p>✗ however with only a comma between two full sentences.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The library was quiet. ______, I could not concentrate because I was very tired.</p>\n<p>A. However B. Therefore C. For example D. In addition</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> First idea: the library was quiet (good for studying).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Second idea: I could not concentrate (an unexpected result).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> An unexpected contrast needs However.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">النتيجة عكس المتوقع فنستخدم However.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which word or phrase best fills the blank?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Many Saudi cities are growing quickly. ______, Riyadh's population has more than doubled since the 1990s.</p>\n<p>A. However B. Otherwise C. For example D. In contrast</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> First idea: many cities are growing (general).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Second idea: Riyadh's population doubled (one specific case).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A specific case needs For example.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحالة المحددة تحتاج For example.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence uses the transition correctly?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. It was very hot, therefore we stayed inside.</p>\n<p>B. It was very hot; therefore, we stayed inside.</p>\n<p>C. It was very hot therefore, we stayed inside.</p>\n<p>D. It was very hot; therefore we, stayed inside.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> therefore joins two full sentences.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> It needs a full stop or a semicolon before it and a comma after it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only the answer with a semicolon before therefore and a comma after it is punctuated correctly.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تحقق من الترقيم قبل therefore وبعدها.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B1-03 — Social media and students: advantages and disadvantages</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a paragraph of 100–150 words about the advantages and disadvantages of social media for students. Use at least five transitions from different groups (addition, contrast, result, example).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب فقرة من مئة إلى مئة وخمسين كلمة عن مزايا وسائل التواصل الاجتماعي وعيوبها للطلاب، واستخدم خمس أدوات انتقال على الأقل من مجموعات مختلفة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: social media has both advantages and disadvantages.</p>\n<p>2. On the one hand, … (advantage 1 + For example, …)</p>\n<p>3. In addition, … (advantage 2)</p>\n<p>4. On the other hand, … (disadvantage 1 + as a result, …)</p>\n<p>5. Furthermore, … (disadvantage 2)</p>\n<p>6. Nevertheless, … (your balanced conclusion)</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (109 words; target 100–150)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Social media has both advantages and disadvantages for students. On the one hand, it can support learning. For example, students can join study groups, share notes and follow educational accounts that explain difficult topics. In addition, it helps them stay in touch with friends and family. On the other hand, social media can cause serious problems. Many students spend hours scrolling instead of studying, and as a result, their grades may fall. Furthermore, some content online is false or harmful. Nevertheless, social media is not bad in itself. If students limit their time online and choose useful content, they can enjoy its benefits while avoiding most of its dangers.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ Transitions from every group guide the reader: For example, In addition, On the other hand, as a result, Furthermore, Nevertheless.</p>\n<p>▸ On the one hand … On the other hand clearly divides advantages and disadvantages.</p>\n<p>▸ Each transition is punctuated correctly with a comma after it.</p>\n<p>▸ The final sentences give a balanced opinion instead of just repeating the points.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Did I use transitions from at least four different groups?</p>\n<p>☐ Does each transition match the relationship between the ideas?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I put a comma after However, Therefore, In addition and similar words?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I avoid although + but and despite + a full clause?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 100–150 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من استخدام أدوات انتقال من مجموعات مختلفة تناسب العلاقة بين الأفكار، ومن الترقيم الصحيح بعدها.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 C · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","However","For instance","Moreover"],"x":["Online shopping is convenient. ______, it can be risky if you use unsafe websites."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] However — convenient / risky is a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج However."},{"n":2,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["However","For example","In contrast","As a result"],"x":["The museum offers free entry on Fridays. ______, it is usually very crowded on that day."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] As a result — The crowds are the result of free entry.","h":"الازدحام نتيجة للدخول المجاني."},{"n":3,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["In addition","However","Instead","For instance"],"x":["Fruit contains many vitamins. ______, it is rich in fibre."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] In addition — A second benefit is added.","h":"إضافة فائدة ثانية."},{"n":4,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["however","for example","therefore","in addition"],"x":["Some animals are active at night. Owls and bats, ______, hunt in the dark."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] for example — Owls and bats are examples of night animals.","h":"البوم والخفافيش أمثلة."},{"n":5,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Although","Because","Since","So"],"x":["______ it was raining heavily, the farmers continued working in the fields."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Although — Rain / continued working is a contrast inside one sentence.","h":"تضاد داخل جملة واحدة."},{"n":6,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["because","so that","whereas","therefore"],"x":["My older brother prefers living in the city, ______ my younger brother loves the quiet of the countryside."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] whereas — whereas compares two opposite preferences.","h":"whereas للمقارنة بين نقيضين."},{"n":7,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Consequently","Nevertheless","For instance","Similarly"],"x":["The company introduced flexible working hours. ______, employees became happier and more productive."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] Consequently — Happier employees are the result.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج Consequently."},{"n":8,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["moreover","otherwise","for example","therefore"],"x":["You should leave now; ______, you will miss the last train."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] otherwise — otherwise means 'if you do not'.","h":"otherwise بمعنى وإلا."},{"n":9,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Although","Because","However","Despite"],"x":["______ the heat, thousands of fans watched the match in the open stadium."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Despite — Despite is followed by a noun (the heat).","h":"despite يليها اسم."},{"n":10,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["On the contrary","In this way","For instance","Despite this"],"x":["Instead of buying new books, many students borrow them from the library. ______, they save a lot of money."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] In this way — Saving money is the result of borrowing.","h":"التوفير نتيجة للاستعارة."},{"n":11,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","Therefore","In fact","For example"],"x":["Many people believe that cats are unfriendly. ______, cats can be very loving and loyal pets."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] In fact — In fact corrects a common belief.","h":"In fact لتصحيح اعتقاد."},{"n":12,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Nevertheless","Otherwise","Furthermore","In contrast"],"x":["Regular exercise strengthens the heart. ______, it improves mental health by reducing stress."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] Furthermore — A second benefit is added.","h":"إضافة فائدة أخرى."},{"n":13,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","Moreover","For instance","Nevertheless"],"x":["The new phone is expensive. ______, many people are buying it because of its excellent camera."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Nevertheless — expensive / many people buying it is a surprising contrast.","h":"تضاد مفاجئ."},{"n":14,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["such as","as a result","in contrast","although"],"x":["Saudi Arabia is investing in renewable energy ______ solar and wind power."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] such as — such as introduces examples (nouns).","h":"such as تقدم أمثلة."},{"n":15,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["However","In addition","Otherwise","Therefore"],"x":["Ahmed did not revise for the test. ______, he got a low mark."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Therefore — The low mark is the result.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج Therefore."},{"n":16,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["on the other hand","as a result","for instance","furthermore"],"x":["Some students prefer to study alone. Others, ______, find that studying in groups helps them understand difficult ideas."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] on the other hand — Two groups with opposite preferences.","h":"مجموعتان بتفضيلين متعاكسين."},{"n":17,"s":"(A) Although the road was (B) busy, (C) but we (D) arrived on time.","o":["Although","busy","but","arrived"],"k":2,"e":"[error] but — although and but cannot be used together; remove but.","h":"لا تجتمع although مع but."},{"n":18,"s":"He trained (A) every day. (B) Despite (C) of this, he (D) lost the final.","o":["every day","Despite","of","lost"],"k":2,"e":"[error] of — We say Despite this, not Despite of this.","h":"نقول Despite this دون of."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence uses the transition correctly?","o":["The shop was closed, however the café next to it was open.","The shop was closed however, the café next to it was open.","The shop was closed; however the café, next to it was open.","The shop was closed; however, the café next to it was open."],"k":3,"e":"[error] The shop was closed; however, the café next to it was open. — Semicolon before however and a comma after it.","h":"فاصلة منقوطة قبل however وفاصلة بعدها."},{"n":20,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["On the other hand","For example","Therefore","In addition"],"x":["Many young people want to study abroad. They believe it will improve their language skills and give them international experience. ______, studying abroad can be expensive and lonely, so students should prepare carefully before they go."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector] On the other hand — The paragraph turns from advantages to disadvantages.","h":"انتقال من المزايا إلى العيوب."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Social media can help students in their studies. (2) They can join study groups and share notes. (3) They can follow educational pages and experts. (4) Some celebrities have millions of followers. (5) They can also ask classmates questions quickly. (6) Used wisely, social media can be a useful learning tool."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Celebrities' followers do not show how social media helps study.","h":"متابعو المشاهير لا يدعمون فكرة الدراسة."},{"n":22,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","2 – 3 – 4 – 1"],"x":["(1) Therefore, it is important to check information before sharing it.","(2) The internet contains a huge amount of information.","(3) However, not all of it is accurate.","(4) Some websites publish false news to attract readers."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — topic → However → example → Therefore.","h":"موضوع ثم تضاد ثم مثال ثم نتيجة."},{"n":23,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Remote villages are often very small.","Doctors work in hospitals.","The internet allows people to work across long distances.","Business meetings can be long."],"x":["______ Doctors can monitor patients' health from far away. Teachers can share lessons with students in remote villages. Businesses can hold meetings without travelling."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The internet allows people to work across long distances. — Each detail shows work done from a distance.","h":"كل تفصيلة عمل عن بعد."},{"n":24,"s":"Neither the teacher (A) nor the students (B) was (C) aware of the (D) change.","o":["nor","was","aware","change"],"k":1,"e":"[error] was — With neither … nor, the verb agrees with the nearer subject (the students): were.","h":"الفعل يطابق الفاعل الأقرب."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Clothes are sold in every shopping mall.","Some people buy new clothes every week.","Water is used in many industries.","Clearly, the true cost of cheap clothing is much higher than its price."],"x":["Fast fashion allows people to buy cheap clothes very often. However, many of these clothes are thrown away after a few months. Producing them uses huge amounts of water and energy. Workers in some factories also receive very low wages. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] Clearly, the true cost of cheap clothing is much higher than its price. — The conclusion sums up all the hidden costs.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص التكاليف الخفية."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["My mother is an excellent cook.","Moreover, I have learned to plan meals and shop for ingredients.","Restaurants in our city are expensive.","Some meals take hours to prepare."],"x":["Learning to cook has made me more independent. I can prepare simple meals when my parents are busy. ______ I also feel proud when my family enjoys my food."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Moreover, I have learned to plan meals and shop for ingredients. — The gap adds another way cooking made the writer independent.","h":"إضافة جانب آخر للاستقلالية."},{"n":27,"s":"Which phrase is the most formal way to begin a sentence that presents an opposing view?","o":["Some guys think that …","Loads of people reckon …","Whatever others say, …","Some people argue that …"],"k":3,"e":"[word choice / register] Some people argue that … — Some people argue that … is formal and neutral.","h":"عبارة رسمية محايدة."},{"n":28,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["Although she was tired, she finished her project.","Although she was tired, but she finished her project.","She was tired, although, she finished her project.","Although she was tired. She finished her project."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Although she was tired, she finished her project. — although-part + comma + main idea.","h":"although ثم فاصلة ثم الفكرة الرئيسة."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 5 – 4","2 – 3 – 5 – 1 – 4","3 – 2 – 5 – 1 – 4","2 – 5 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) Then add the vegetables and cook for ten minutes.","(2) Kabsa is a traditional Saudi rice dish.","(3) To make it, first fry the onions in oil.","(4) Finally, add the rice and water, and cook until the rice is soft.","(5) Next, add the chicken and the spices."],"k":1,"e":"[best order] 2 – 3 – 5 – 1 – 4 — topic → first → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"موضوع ثم خطوات بالترتيب."},{"n":30,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","Even so","For instance","Similarly"],"x":["The test was difficult. ______, most students passed it."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector] Even so — difficult / most passed is a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج Even so."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"3.4","t":"Completing a Paragraph (The Best Sentence for the Gap)","html":"<p><strong>Unit 3 · Lesson 3.4 · CEFR B1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use the sentences before and after a gap to choose the best sentence.</p>\n<p>2. Reject options that break unity or coherence.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب الجمل قبل الفراغ وبعده لاختيار أفضل جملة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يرفض البدائل التي تكسر وحدة الفقرة أو ترابطها.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>In complete-the-paragraph items, one sentence is missing from the middle of a paragraph. The correct sentence must fit in THREE ways: it must stay on the TOPIC (unity), it must CONNECT logically to the sentence before the gap, and it must PREPARE for the sentence after the gap (coherence).</p>\n<p>The sentence AFTER the gap is often the key. Look at its first words. If it starts with However, the gap must say something that the next sentence contrasts with. If it starts with For example, the gap must make a general point. If it starts with As a result, Therefore or Because of this, the gap must give a cause. If it contains this, these, it or they, the gap must contain the thing that the pronoun refers to.</p>\n<p>Wrong options are usually: (1) TRUE but off-topic sentences (The Red Sea lies between Africa and Asia); (2) sentences on the topic that do not connect to the next sentence; (3) sentences that contradict the paragraph; and (4) sentences that repeat a key word but say something different. Read your choice in place: the paragraph should flow without any jump.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>after = However</strong> Tablets are light and store many books. ______ However, some teachers worry about games. → the gap gives another advantage</p>\n<p><strong>after = For example</strong> ______ For example, students can save part of their pocket money. → the gap gives a general point</p>\n<p><strong>after = As a result</strong> ______ As a result, some cities have strict rules. → the gap gives a problem (cause)</p>\n<p><strong>after = This</strong> ______ This food could feed millions of people. → the gap must name 'this food'</p>\n<p><strong>after = In fact</strong> ______ In fact, the brain learns more when we correct mistakes. → the gap gives a view that In fact supports or corrects</p>\n<p><strong>✗ true but off</strong> The Red Sea lies between Africa and Asia. (true, but does not connect to 'them' = the reefs)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ contradiction</strong> Some people never make mistakes. (goes against the paragraph)</p>\n<p><strong>test</strong> Read the sentence before + your choice + the sentence after: is there a jump?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في أسئلة إكمال الفقرة تنقص جملة من وسط الفقرة، ويجب أن تناسب الجملة الصحيحة ثلاثة أمور: البقاء في الموضوع، والارتباط بما قبل الفراغ، والتمهيد لما بعده. والجملة التي بعد الفراغ هي المفتاح غالبًا: إن بدأت بـ However فالفراغ يحتاج فكرة تخالفها، وإن بدأت بـ For example فالفراغ يحتاج فكرة عامة، وإن بدأت بـ As a result فالفراغ يحتاج سببًا، وإن احتوت على this أو it فالفراغ يحتاج ما يعود إليه الضمير.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the topic sentence and write the controlling idea.</p>\n<p>2. Read the sentence AFTER the gap and underline its first words and any pronouns.</p>\n<p>3. Decide what the gap must do: give a cause, a general point, a contrast, a noun for a pronoun, or the next step.</p>\n<p>4. Eliminate options that are off-topic, contradictory or unconnected.</p>\n<p>5. Read the three sentences together (before + choice + after) to check the flow.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ جملة الموضوع وحدد الفكرة المسيطرة، واقرأ الجملة التي بعد الفراغ وضع خطًا تحت كلماتها الأولى وضمائرها، وحدد وظيفة الفراغ، واستبعد البدائل الخارجة عن الموضوع أو المتناقضة أو غير المرتبطة، ثم اقرأ الجمل الثلاث معًا.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A true fact about the subject that does not connect to the next sentence.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that ignores the signal word after the gap (However, For example, As a result).</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that has no noun for the pronoun in the next sentence.</p>\n<p>✗ A sentence that contradicts the writer's point.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our class planned a trip to the desert. We prepared food, tents and warm clothes. ______ In the end, we postponed the trip until the following weekend.</p>\n<p>A. The desert is beautiful at night.</p>\n<p>B. Tents can be bought in most sports shops.</p>\n<p>C. Unfortunately, the weather forecast warned of a strong sandstorm.</p>\n<p>D. Our teacher had organized many trips before.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Before the gap: the class prepared for the trip. After the gap: they postponed it.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The gap must give a reason for the change.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only the sandstorm warning explains the postponement.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة التي بعد الفراغ نتيجة، فالفراغ يحتاج سببًا.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Coffee was first drunk in Yemen more than five hundred years ago. ______ Today, it is one of the most popular drinks in the world.</p>\n<p>A. Coffee contains caffeine, which keeps people awake.</p>\n<p>B. From there, it spread to Makkah, Cairo and Istanbul, and later to Europe.</p>\n<p>C. Many people prefer tea to coffee.</p>\n<p>D. Yemen is a country in the south of the Arabian Peninsula.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The paragraph moves in time: first drunk in Yemen → Today, popular worldwide.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The gap must show how coffee travelled from Yemen to the world.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'From there, it spread …' connects both sentences.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفقرة زمنية، والفراغ يحتاج مرحلة الانتشار.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Many people believe that you need expensive equipment to exercise. ______ For example, walking, running and push-ups are free and can be done almost anywhere.</p>\n<p>A. Gyms usually charge a monthly fee.</p>\n<p>B. Professional athletes train every day.</p>\n<p>C. Running shoes can be very expensive.</p>\n<p>D. In reality, some of the best exercises need no equipment at all.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> After the gap: For example, free exercises.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> So the gap needs a general idea that those examples support.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'some of the best exercises need no equipment' is that idea.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأمثلة بعد الفراغ تدعم فكرة عامة يجب أن تكون في الفراغ.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B1-04 — Why sleep matters for students</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a paragraph of 100–150 words explaining why sleep matters for students. Make sure each sentence connects clearly to the sentence before and after it.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب فقرة من مئة إلى مئة وخمسين كلمة تشرح فيها أهمية النوم للطلاب، وتأكد من أن كل جملة ترتبط بوضوح بما قبلها وما بعدها.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: sleep is as important as studying.</p>\n<p>2. First reason: memory + explanation.</p>\n<p>3. Second reason: concentration + evidence.</p>\n<p>4. In addition: health and mood.</p>\n<p>5. The problem: why many students do not sleep enough.</p>\n<p>6. Solution and concluding sentence.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (127 words; target 100–150)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sleep is just as important for students as studying. First, sleep helps the brain store new information. When students sleep, the brain organizes what they learned during the day, so they remember it better in exams. Second, sleep affects concentration. Students who sleep less than seven hours often find it difficult to pay attention in class and make more careless mistakes. In addition, a lack of sleep can affect health and mood. Tired students are more likely to get ill and feel irritable or anxious. Unfortunately, many students stay up late using their phones. To get the sleep they need, they should switch off screens an hour before bed and keep a regular routine. Good sleep is one of the simplest ways to do better at school.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ Each reason is followed by a sentence that explains or proves it.</p>\n<p>▸ Signal words (First, Second, In addition, Unfortunately) connect the ideas smoothly.</p>\n<p>▸ Pronouns (it, they) always refer clearly to nouns before them.</p>\n<p>▸ The paragraph moves from reasons to a problem and a solution, then concludes.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does every sentence connect to the one before it?</p>\n<p>☐ Does every sentence prepare for the one after it?</p>\n<p>☐ Is each reason explained with a detail or example?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use signal words to show the relationships?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 100–150 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اقرأ كل ثلاث جمل متتالية وتأكد من عدم وجود قفزة في الأفكار.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 B · Example 3 D","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Textbooks were first printed hundreds of years ago.","Some tablets are more expensive than laptops.","Teachers have used blackboards for a long time.","They also allow students to watch videos and do interactive exercises."],"x":["Many schools now use tablets instead of textbooks. Tablets are light and can store hundreds of books. ______ However, some teachers worry that students get distracted by games and social media."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They also allow students to watch videos and do interactive exercises. — However needs another advantage before it.","h":"However تحتاج ميزة أخرى قبلها."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Fewer than two hundred are thought to live in the wild today.","Leopards are bigger than domestic cats.","Many animals live in the Arabian Peninsula.","Some zoos have lions and tigers."],"x":["The Arabian leopard is one of the rarest animals in the world. ______ To protect it, Saudi Arabia has started a programme to breed leopards and return them to the wild."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Fewer than two hundred are thought to live in the wild today. — The gap shows how rare it is, which explains the need to protect it.","h":"الجملة تبين ندرته فتفسر الحماية."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Money is printed by the central bank.","Fortunately, there are simple ways to start practising it early.","Teenagers often buy clothes and games.","Some adults earn a lot of money."],"x":["Learning to manage money is an important skill for teenagers. ______ For example, they can save part of their pocket money each week and keep track of what they spend."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Fortunately, there are simple ways to start practising it early. — For example needs a general point about ways to practise.","h":"For example تحتاج فكرة عامة."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Rice is the most popular food in Saudi Arabia.","Sugar is bad for our teeth.","My grandfather was born in a small village.","Over the years, he added more products and opened a second branch."],"x":["My grandfather started his small shop in 1975. At first, he sold only rice, sugar and tea. ______ Today, the shop is run by my father and is one of the biggest supermarkets in our town."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Over the years, he added more products and opened a second branch. — The gap bridges 'At first' and 'Today'.","h":"الجملة تربط بين البداية واليوم."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Big cities offer many job opportunities.","Some people enjoy loud music.","Traffic, construction work and loud music can be heard day and night.","Hearing tests are done in hospitals."],"x":["Noise pollution is a growing problem in big cities. ______ Studies show that long exposure to noise can cause stress, sleep problems and even hearing loss."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Traffic, construction work and loud music can be heard day and night. — The gap describes the noise before its effects are explained.","h":"الجملة تصف الضوضاء قبل آثارها."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Mistakes in exams can lower your mark.","Some people never make mistakes.","Scientists work in laboratories.","However, mistakes are an important part of learning."],"x":["Many people think that making mistakes is a bad thing. ______ In fact, scientists say that the brain learns more when we correct our mistakes."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] However, mistakes are an important part of learning. — The gap gives the writer's opposite view, which In fact then supports.","h":"الجملة تقدم رأي الكاتب الذي تدعمه In fact."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Life was simple, and many families had very little money.","Oil is used to make petrol and plastic.","Fishing is still popular in coastal cities.","Many countries produce oil today."],"x":["Before the discovery of oil, most people in Arabia worked in farming, fishing or trade. ______ After oil was discovered in the 1930s, the economy changed completely."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Life was simple, and many families had very little money. — The gap continues describing life before oil.","h":"الجملة تكمل وصف الحياة قبل النفط."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The old library was built fifty years ago.","Children's books are usually colourful.","Cafés are popular with young people.","It also offers free internet and quiet study rooms."],"x":["The new public library in our city is very modern. It has a large children's section and a café. ______ Because of this, many students now go there to do their homework in the evening."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] It also offers free internet and quiet study rooms. — Because of this needs a reason that attracts students who do homework.","h":"Because of this تحتاج سببًا يجذب الطلاب."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Many teenagers like to stay up late on weekends.","Adults usually need less sleep than babies.","Doctors recommend that they sleep between eight and ten hours a night.","Some people sleep better in a cool room."],"x":["Getting enough sleep is essential for teenagers. ______ Without it, they may feel tired, find it hard to concentrate and get ill more often."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Doctors recommend that they sleep between eight and ten hours a night. — 'Without it' refers to the recommended amount of sleep.","h":"Without it تعود إلى قدر النوم الموصى به."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Many people enjoy cooking at home.","Some food is imported from other countries.","Healthy food can be expensive.","Every year, about one third of all food produced is thrown away."],"x":["Wasting food is a serious problem. ______ This food could feed millions of hungry people around the world."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Every year, about one third of all food produced is thrown away. — 'This food' refers to the wasted food in the gap.","h":"This food تعود إلى الطعام المهدر."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Many people are afraid of spiders.","My teacher encouraged me to practise in front of my family every evening.","Presentations are part of most school subjects.","Ten-year-olds are usually in Grade 4."],"x":["When I was ten, I was afraid of speaking in front of the class. My hands shook, and I forgot my words. ______ Now I enjoy giving presentations and even took part in a public speaking competition."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] My teacher encouraged me to practise in front of my family every evening. — The gap explains how the fear changed into enjoyment.","h":"الجملة تشرح كيف تغيّر الخوف."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Their thick mud walls kept out the heat of the sun.","Modern houses use air conditioners.","Many tourists visit old villages.","Mud is made from earth and water."],"x":["Traditional Saudi houses were designed to stay cool. ______ In addition, wind towers on the roofs caught the breeze and sent it down into the rooms."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Their thick mud walls kept out the heat of the sun. — In addition needs a first cooling feature before it.","h":"In addition تحتاج ميزة أولى للتبريد."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Scooters were invented more than a hundred years ago.","Many cities have good public transport.","However, they can be dangerous when riders use the pavement or leave them in the middle of the road.","Some riders use them to go to work."],"x":["Electric scooters have become popular in many cities. They are cheap to rent and easy to ride. ______ As a result, some cities have introduced strict rules about where they can be used and parked."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] However, they can be dangerous when riders use the pavement or leave them in the middle of the road. — As a result needs a problem that causes the strict rules.","h":"As a result تحتاج مشكلة قبلها."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Music is taught in many schools.","They say it helps them relax and concentrate.","Homework should not take more than two hours.","Some songs are very long."],"x":["Some students believe that they can do their homework while listening to music. ______ Others, however, find that music distracts them and prefer complete silence."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] They say it helps them relax and concentrate. — The gap explains the first group's view before 'Others, however'.","h":"الجملة تشرح رأي المجموعة الأولى."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The Red Sea lies between Africa and Asia.","These reefs are home to more than a thousand kinds of fish.","Many tourists enjoy swimming in pools.","Fish are an important source of protein."],"x":["The Red Sea is famous for its coral reefs. ______ Unfortunately, rising sea temperatures and pollution are damaging some of them."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] These reefs are home to more than a thousand kinds of fish. — 'some of them' refers to the reefs, so the gap must continue about the reefs.","h":"them تعود إلى الشعاب."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Teams are common in sports such as football.","Some people prefer working alone.","Most companies have more than one team.","If they do not listen to each other, conflicts can quickly develop."],"x":["Working in a team is not always easy. Team members may have different opinions and ways of working. ______ Therefore, good communication is the key to successful teamwork."],"k":3,"e":"[complete the paragraph] If they do not listen to each other, conflicts can quickly develop. — Therefore needs a problem that communication can solve.","h":"Therefore تحتاج مشكلة يحلها التواصل."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Thursday is the last day of the school week.","Teachers read many books at university.","Since the programme started, the number of books borrowed from the library has doubled.","Book clubs are popular in many countries."],"x":["Our school introduced a 'reading hour' every Thursday. During this hour, everyone in the school, including teachers, reads a book of their choice. ______ Several students have even started their own book clubs."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] Since the programme started, the number of books borrowed from the library has doubled. — The gap shows a result of the programme, and 'even' adds a bigger one.","h":"الجملة نتيجة للبرنامج وeven تضيف نتيجة أكبر."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["As a result, cities are growing quickly and becoming more crowded.","Villages are usually quieter than cities.","Many jobs require a university degree.","Some cities have very tall buildings."],"x":["Many people are moving from villages to big cities to find work. ______ On the other hand, villages are losing young people, and some are becoming almost empty."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] As a result, cities are growing quickly and becoming more crowded. — The gap gives the effect on cities, contrasted with the effect on villages.","h":"أثر الهجرة على المدن مقابل القرى."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Some old books are kept in museums.","With the printing press, hundreds of copies could be made in a short time.","Handwriting was taught in schools.","Paper was invented in China."],"x":["The invention of the printing press changed the world. Before it, books were copied by hand, which took months. ______ This meant that knowledge could spread much faster than ever before."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph] With the printing press, hundreds of copies could be made in a short time. — 'This meant' needs the change that the press brought.","h":"This meant تحتاج التغيير الذي أحدثته المطبعة."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Children usually ask for toys and games.","Happy children often do well at school.","However, children who always get what they want may find it difficult to deal with disappointment later in life.","Some parents work very long hours."],"x":["Some parents give their children everything they ask for. They believe this will make their children happy. ______ Experts suggest that children should learn to wait and to work for the things they want."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] However, children who always get what they want may find it difficult to deal with disappointment later in life. — The gap gives the problem that the experts' advice answers.","h":"الجملة تقدم المشكلة التي تعالجها النصيحة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) Cycling to school has many benefits. (2) It is good exercise and helps students stay fit. (3) Bicycles come in many different colours and sizes. (4) It reduces traffic around schools in the morning. (5) It also helps students arrive feeling awake and ready to learn. (6) Schools should provide safe places for students to park their bikes."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 3 — Colours and sizes of bicycles are not a benefit of cycling to school.","h":"ألوان الدراجات ليست فائدة."},{"n":22,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Moreover","Nevertheless","For instance","Therefore"],"x":["The museum was closed for repairs. ______, we visited the old market instead."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] Therefore — Visiting the market is the result of the museum being closed.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج Therefore."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 5 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 5 – 4","1 – 2 – 3 – 5 – 4","2 – 1 – 5 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) He decided to start a small business selling handmade bags online.","(2) Ibrahim lost his job last year.","(3) At first, he received only a few orders each month.","(4) Now he employs five people and sells to customers in three countries.","(5) However, after he improved his website, sales increased quickly."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 3 – 5 – 4 — lost job → started business → At first → However, improved → Now.","h":"مشكلة ثم بداية ثم تحسن ثم الحاضر."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Exams are stressful for many students.","Some topics are more difficult than others.","Doing practice tests before an exam is very useful.","Teachers write tests at the end of each unit."],"x":["______ First, it helps you remember what you have learned. Second, it shows you which topics you need to study again. Finally, it reduces stress because you know what to expect."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Doing practice tests before an exam is very useful. — The reasons explain the usefulness of practice tests.","h":"الأسباب تشرح فائدة الاختبارات التجريبية."},{"n":25,"s":"The number of students who (A) walk to school (B) have (C) increased (D) this year.","o":["walk","have","increased","this year"],"k":1,"e":"[error] have — The subject is 'The number', which is singular: has increased.","h":"الفاعل The number مفرد."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["These old skills are clearly finding a new place in modern life.","Pottery is made from clay.","Online shopping is growing quickly.","Some young people prefer video games."],"x":["In many parts of the world, young people are learning traditional crafts again. They take classes in pottery, weaving and woodwork. Some sell their products online and earn good money. Others simply enjoy making something beautiful with their hands. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] These old skills are clearly finding a new place in modern life. — The conclusion sums up the return of traditional crafts.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص عودة الحرف التقليدية."},{"n":27,"s":"Which word best completes the formal sentence: 'The government has ______ a new law to protect wildlife.'?","o":["put in","introduced","made up","got"],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] introduced — introduce a law is the correct formal collocation.","h":"introduce a law تعبير رسمي صحيح."},{"n":28,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["Despite the bad weather, the event was a great success.","Despite the weather was bad, the event was a great success.","Despite of the bad weather, the event was a great success.","Although the bad weather, the event was a great success."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Despite the bad weather, the event was a great success. — Despite + noun phrase, without of.","h":"Despite يليها اسم دون of."},{"n":29,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","For example","Furthermore","In contrast"],"x":["Some people prefer e-books because they are light and easy to carry. ______, others still prefer printed books because they enjoy the feel of paper."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] In contrast — Two groups with opposite preferences.","h":"تفضيلان متعاكسان."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Saudi Arabia's Vision 2030 aims to diversify the economy. (2) The country wants to depend less on oil. (3) It is developing new industries, such as tourism and entertainment. (4) It is also investing in technology and renewable energy. (5) More women are joining the workforce. (6) Oil prices often change from month to month. (7) These changes are creating many new jobs for young Saudis."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 6 — Changing oil prices are not part of the plan to diversify.","h":"تقلب أسعار النفط ليس جزءًا من خطة التنويع."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"3.5","t":"Paragraph Types: Narrative, Descriptive, Opinion","html":"<p><strong>Unit 3 · Lesson 3.5 · CEFR B1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Recognize and write narrative, descriptive and opinion paragraphs.</p>\n<p>2. Choose topic and concluding sentences that suit each paragraph type.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يتعرف الطالب على الفقرة السردية والوصفية والفقرة التي تعبر عن رأي ويكتبها.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار جمل الموضوع والجمل الختامية المناسبة لكل نوع.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>A NARRATIVE paragraph tells a story in time order. Its topic sentence introduces the event and often hints at its meaning (My first public speaking competition taught me never to give up). Its conclusion usually gives the result or a lesson learned (I will never forget the honesty of that stranger). Narratives use the past tense and time words: suddenly, then, in the end.</p>\n<p>A DESCRIPTIVE paragraph paints a picture of a person, place or thing. Its topic sentence gives an overall impression (The old market is always busy and full of life), and the supporting sentences use the five senses: sight, sound, smell, touch and taste, often in space order. Its conclusion returns to the overall impression or the writer's feeling. An OPINION paragraph gives the writer's view and supports it with reasons. Its topic sentence states the opinion clearly (In my opinion, every school should have a garden), and its conclusion restates the opinion, often with For these reasons or In conclusion.</p>\n<p>In STEP, topic- and concluding-sentence items often test whether you notice the TYPE of paragraph. In a story, a general piece of advice is not the best topic sentence. In a description, a sentence that tells an event (Last year, we drove to Abha) does not fit. In an opinion paragraph, a fact that everyone agrees with (Homework is given in most schools) is not a strong topic sentence, and a conclusion must not contradict the writer's view.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>narrative TS</strong> Last summer, our family trip turned into a frightening adventure.</p>\n<p><strong>narrative CS</strong> It was the hardest walk of our lives, but every step was worth it.</p>\n<p><strong>descriptive TS</strong> The inside of the mosque is calm and magnificent.</p>\n<p><strong>descriptive senses</strong> The smell of fresh bread and Arabic coffee comes from small cafés.</p>\n<p><strong>opinion TS</strong> In my view, homework is useful if it is not excessive.</p>\n<p><strong>opinion CS</strong> For these reasons, first aid should be part of every school's programme.</p>\n<p><strong>✗ mismatch</strong> Cars need regular checks. (advice, not the start of a story)</p>\n<p><strong>✗ mismatch</strong> Students should never have homework. (contradicts the writer's balanced opinion)</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفقرة السردية تحكي قصة بترتيب زمني، وتقدم جملة موضوعها الحدث وتلمح إلى معناه، وتنتهي بنتيجة أو درس مستفاد. والفقرة الوصفية ترسم صورة لشخص أو مكان، وتعطي جملة موضوعها انطباعًا عامًا، وتستخدم الحواس الخمس. والفقرة التي تعبر عن رأي تذكر رأي الكاتب وتدعمه بالأسباب، وتعيد خاتمتها الرأي. وفي الاختبار تُختبر قدرتك على ملاحظة نوع الفقرة: فالنصيحة لا تناسب بداية القصة، والحدث لا يناسب الوصف، والحقيقة المتفق عليها ليست جملة رأي قوية.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Read the supporting sentences and decide the type: story (past events), description (senses, places) or opinion (reasons, I believe).</p>\n<p>2. For a narrative, choose a topic sentence that introduces the event; for a description, an overall impression; for an opinion, a clear view.</p>\n<p>3. For conclusions, choose a lesson or result (narrative), a feeling or impression (descriptive), or a restated opinion (opinion).</p>\n<p>4. Reject facts, advice or events that do not match the paragraph type.</p>\n<p>5. Check that an opinion conclusion agrees with the writer's view in the paragraph.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدد نوع الفقرة من الجمل الداعمة، واختر للسرد جملة تقدم الحدث، وللوصف انطباعًا عامًا، وللرأي موقفًا واضحًا، واختر للخاتمة درسًا أو نتيجة أو شعورًا أو إعادة للرأي، وارفض ما لا يناسب نوع الفقرة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A piece of advice offered as the topic sentence of a story.</p>\n<p>✗ An event offered as the topic sentence of a description.</p>\n<p>✗ A neutral fact offered as the topic sentence of an opinion paragraph.</p>\n<p>✗ A conclusion that contradicts the writer's opinion.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Which sentence would make the best topic sentence for a DESCRIPTIVE paragraph about a market?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Yesterday, I went to the fish market with my uncle.</p>\n<p>B. The fish market in Jeddah is noisy, colourful and full of interesting smells.</p>\n<p>C. I think fish markets should be cleaner.</p>\n<p>D. Fish is healthier than red meat.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Descriptive = an overall picture of a place.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'Yesterday, I went …' starts a story; 'I think … should be cleaner' is an opinion; the last option is a general fact.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Only 'noisy, colourful and full of interesting smells' describes the place.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">جملة الوصف تقدم انطباعًا عن المكان بالحواس.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Last year, I forgot my bag on the bus. Inside were my phone, my keys and my wallet. I called the bus company, but they said nothing had been found. Two days later, a man knocked on our door. He had found my bag and brought it back with everything inside. ______</p>\n<p>A. Buses in our city are blue and white.</p>\n<p>B. Wallets should be kept in a safe pocket.</p>\n<p>C. Bus companies have lost-and-found offices.</p>\n<p>D. I will never forget the honesty of that stranger.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> This is a narrative: a story in the past.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> A good ending gives the meaning of the story.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> 'I will never forget the honesty of that stranger' does this; the others are facts or advice.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: D</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">خاتمة القصة تبين معنى الحدث.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>______ First, it allows students to choose subjects that match their interests. Second, it prepares them for university, where they will have to make their own decisions. Of course, they still need guidance from teachers and parents.</p>\n<p>A. In my opinion, secondary students should be allowed to choose more of their subjects.</p>\n<p>B. Secondary school lasts three years.</p>\n<p>C. University students study many subjects.</p>\n<p>D. Teachers give advice to students every day.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The paragraph gives reasons: it is an opinion paragraph.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The topic sentence must state the opinion that the reasons support.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The other options are neutral facts.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">فقرة الرأي تبدأ بجملة تذكر الرأي بوضوح.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B1-05 — Describing a historic place in Saudi Arabia</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write a descriptive paragraph of 100–150 words about a historic place in Saudi Arabia. Begin with an overall impression and use at least three of the five senses.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب فقرة وصفية من مئة إلى مئة وخمسين كلمة عن مكان تاريخي في المملكة العربية السعودية، وابدأ بانطباع عام واستخدم ثلاث حواس على الأقل.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: name the place and your overall impression.</p>\n<p>2. Sight: buildings, colours, materials.</p>\n<p>3. Special features: what makes it unique?</p>\n<p>4. Smell and sound: what can you smell and hear?</p>\n<p>5. A fact about its history or importance.</p>\n<p>6. Concluding sentence: your feeling or the impression it leaves.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (112 words; target 100–150)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Al-Balad, the historic heart of Jeddah, is one of the most charming places in Saudi Arabia. Its narrow streets are lined with tall houses built of coral stone, some of them more than three hundred years old. The most beautiful features are the wooden windows and balconies, called rawasheen, which are painted in shades of green, blue and brown. As you walk, you can smell spices and fresh bread from the busy old market. In the evening, lanterns light up the alleys, and the sound of the call to prayer echoes between the buildings. In 2014, Al-Balad was added to UNESCO's World Heritage List. Visiting it feels like stepping back in time.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ The topic sentence names the place and gives an overall impression (charming).</p>\n<p>▸ Details appeal to sight (coral stone, colours), smell (spices, bread) and sound (the call to prayer).</p>\n<p>▸ One historical fact (UNESCO, 2014) adds authority without turning the paragraph into a history lesson.</p>\n<p>▸ The concluding sentence gives a vivid final impression.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does my topic sentence give an overall impression of the place?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use at least three senses?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use precise adjectives (narrow, coral, wooden) instead of 'nice' or 'good'?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I avoid turning the description into a story or an opinion essay?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 100–150 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تأكد من أن جملتك الأولى انطباع عام، ومن استخدام ثلاث حواس على الأقل وصفات دقيقة، ومن بقاء الفقرة وصفية.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 A","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Last summer, our family trip turned into a frightening adventure.","Cars need regular checks before long journeys.","The desert is very large and empty.","My father is a careful driver."],"x":["______ We were driving through the desert when the car suddenly stopped. My father tried to start the engine, but nothing happened. We had no phone signal and very little water. Finally, after two hours, a family stopped and drove us to the nearest town."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Last summer, our family trip turned into a frightening adventure. — A narrative needs a topic sentence that introduces the event.","h":"السرد يحتاج جملة تقدم الحدث."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Mud bricks are cheap to make.","Many old villages are now empty.","The old village of Ushaiger is one of the most beautiful places I have seen.","Palm trees need a lot of water."],"x":["______ Its walls are made of red mud bricks, and its narrow streets wind between the old houses. Tall palm trees surround the village, and in the evening the golden light makes everything glow."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The old village of Ushaiger is one of the most beautiful places I have seen. — A description needs an overall impression of the place.","h":"الوصف يحتاج انطباعًا عامًا."},{"n":3,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Homework is given in most schools.","Students should never have homework.","Teachers are very busy people.","In my view, homework is useful if it is not excessive."],"x":["______ First, it teaches students to manage their time. Second, it gives them a chance to practise what they learned. However, too much homework can cause stress, so teachers should give a reasonable amount."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] In my view, homework is useful if it is not excessive. — The paragraph gives a balanced opinion, which the topic sentence must state.","h":"الفقرة رأي متوازن."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Many mosques were built centuries ago.","Green is my favourite colour.","Carpets are made in many countries.","The inside of the mosque is calm and magnificent."],"x":["______ It has a high ceiling decorated with green and gold patterns. Thousands of lamps hang from it, and the floor is covered with soft red carpets. The sound of the Quran fills the air."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The inside of the mosque is calm and magnificent. — The sensory details describe the inside of a mosque.","h":"التفاصيل الحسية تصف داخل المسجد."},{"n":5,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Public speaking competitions are held every year.","Judges must be fair to all students.","My first public speaking competition taught me never to give up.","Notes are useful when you give a speech."],"x":["______ I had practised for weeks, but when I stood in front of the judges, my mind went blank. I took a deep breath, looked at my notes and started again slowly. In the end, I won second prize."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] My first public speaking competition taught me never to give up. — The narrative needs an opening that introduces the event and its meaning.","h":"افتتاح السرد يقدم الحدث ومعناه."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Public transport was introduced in Riyadh recently.","Some people cannot afford a car.","Driving is a useful skill.","I strongly believe that public transport is the best way to travel in big cities."],"x":["______ It is cheap, it reduces traffic and it is better for the environment. In addition, people who use it often feel less stressed than drivers. For these reasons, I believe more people should use it."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] I strongly believe that public transport is the best way to travel in big cities. — The reasons support an opinion about public transport.","h":"الأسباب تدعم رأيًا عن النقل العام."},{"n":7,"s":"Which sentence would make the best topic sentence for a DESCRIPTIVE paragraph?","o":["Last year, we drove to Abha and got lost on the way.","The Asir mountains are covered with green terraces and colourful villages.","I think everyone should visit Abha at least once.","Tourism in Abha should be developed further."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The Asir mountains are covered with green terraces and colourful villages. — It gives a picture of a place; the others start a story or give an opinion.","h":"تقدم صورة للمكان."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence would make the best topic sentence for a NARRATIVE paragraph?","o":["Airports are large, busy buildings.","Passports should be kept in a safe place.","The day I lost my passport at the airport was the most stressful day of my life.","In my opinion, airports should have more staff."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The day I lost my passport at the airport was the most stressful day of my life. — It introduces an event to be told as a story.","h":"تقدم حدثًا يُروى."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence would make the best topic sentence for an OPINION paragraph?","o":["Our school garden has roses and palm trees.","In my opinion, every school should have a garden.","Last week, we planted tomatoes in the school garden.","The school garden is next to the playground."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] In my opinion, every school should have a garden. — It states a clear opinion that reasons can support.","h":"تذكر رأيًا واضحًا."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Gold is very expensive this year.","Many people prefer shopping online.","Spices are used in Saudi food.","The old market in the city centre is always busy and full of life."],"x":["______ The streets are full of people from early morning until late at night. Shops sell spices, perfumes, gold and colourful fabrics. The smell of fresh bread and Arabic coffee comes from small cafés."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] The old market in the city centre is always busy and full of life. — The sensory details describe a lively market.","h":"التفاصيل تصف سوقًا مزدحمًا."},{"n":11,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Jabal Sawda is near the city of Abha.","Cold wind can be dangerous for climbers.","It was the hardest walk of our lives, but every step was worth it.","My brother's ankle is now much better."],"x":["Last winter, my brother and I decided to climb Jabal Sawda, the highest mountain in Saudi Arabia. We started early, but the path was steep and the wind was very cold. Halfway up, my brother hurt his ankle, and we had to walk slowly. When we finally reached the top, the view of the clouds below us was incredible. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] It was the hardest walk of our lives, but every step was worth it. — The narrative ends with the meaning of the experience.","h":"القصة تنتهي بمعنى التجربة."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Whenever I visit, I feel calm and happy in her garden.","Lemons are full of vitamin","C. Fountains need regular cleaning.","My grandmother is seventy years old."],"x":["My grandmother's garden is a peaceful place. Roses and jasmine grow along the walls. In the middle, there is a small fountain where birds come to drink. Under a large lemon tree, there is a wooden bench where she reads every afternoon. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] Whenever I visit, I feel calm and happy in her garden. — The description ends with the writer's feeling about the place.","h":"الوصف ينتهي بشعور الكاتب."},{"n":13,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Video games became popular in the 1980s.","In conclusion, video games can be useful if they are played sensibly.","Some games are very expensive.","Teamwork is important in sports too."],"x":["Some people say that video games are a waste of time. I disagree. Many games improve problem-solving and teamwork. Educational games can also teach history, science and languages. Of course, players should not spend too many hours on them. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] In conclusion, video games can be useful if they are played sensibly. — The opinion paragraph ends by restating the balanced view.","h":"فقرة الرأي تنتهي بإعادة الرأي."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["The canteen sells sandwiches and juice.","Football is the most popular sport in my school.","New students often feel nervous.","That boy, Rayan, is still my best friend today."],"x":["On my first day at the new school, I did not know anyone. At lunchtime, I sat alone in the corner of the canteen. Suddenly, a boy from my class came over and asked if he could join me. We talked about football, and by the end of lunch we were laughing together. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] That boy, Rayan, is still my best friend today. — The narrative ends with the result of the event.","h":"القصة تنتهي بنتيجة الحدث."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["It is one of the most breathtaking views in the country.","Riyadh is the capital of Saudi Arabia.","Climbing cliffs can be dangerous.","Sunsets are beautiful in the desert."],"x":["The Edge of the World, near Riyadh, is an amazing natural place. Huge cliffs rise hundreds of metres above a wide, flat plain. From the top, you can see for many kilometres. At sunset, the rocks turn orange and red. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] It is one of the most breathtaking views in the country. — The description ends with an overall impression.","h":"الوصف ينتهي بانطباع عام."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Accidents happen more often in summer.","Doctors study for many years.","For these reasons, first aid should be part of every school's programme.","Some schools have a nurse."],"x":["I believe that students should learn first aid at school. Accidents can happen anywhere, at home, at school or on the road. Knowing what to do in the first few minutes can save a life. Moreover, first aid courses are short and not expensive. ______"],"k":2,"e":"[concluding sentence] For these reasons, first aid should be part of every school's programme. — The opinion is restated after the reasons.","h":"إعادة الرأي بعد الأسباب."},{"n":17,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Ramadan is the ninth month of the Islamic calendar.","Seeing their happy faces made us feel that our effort was truly worthwhile.","Charities need many volunteers.","Food prices rise during Ramadan."],"x":["Last Ramadan, our class decided to help a local charity. We collected food and money from families in our neighbourhood. Then we packed more than two hundred food baskets. On the last Thursday of the month, we delivered them to families in need. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] Seeing their happy faces made us feel that our effort was truly worthwhile. — The narrative ends with the writer's reflection.","h":"القصة تنتهي بتأمل الكاتب."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Light blue is a calming colour.","It is a small room, but it is full of the things I love.","Model planes take a long time to build.","Our garden has three palm trees."],"x":["My bedroom is my favourite place in the house. The walls are painted light blue, and there is a large window that looks out over the garden. Next to the window is my desk, where I study and draw. On the shelves, I keep my books and the model planes I have built. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] It is a small room, but it is full of the things I love. — The description ends by returning to the overall impression.","h":"الوصف يعود إلى الانطباع العام."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Many teenagers work in shops and restaurants.","Studying is the most important thing for students.","Money should be saved in a bank.","As long as it does not affect their studies, a part-time job can be good for teenagers."],"x":["Many people think that teenagers should not have part-time jobs because they need to focus on their studies. However, I believe that a few hours of work each week can be very valuable. Teenagers learn to manage money and time. They also gain confidence and experience that will help them in the future. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence] As long as it does not affect their studies, a part-time job can be good for teenagers. — The conclusion restates the writer's view and its condition.","h":"الخاتمة تعيد رأي الكاتب وشرطه."},{"n":20,"s":"Which sentence would be the best concluding sentence for an OPINION paragraph about school uniforms?","o":["For these reasons, I believe school uniforms should remain compulsory.","Our school uniform is grey and white.","Last year, I lost my school tie.","Uniforms are sold in many shops."],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence] For these reasons, I believe school uniforms should remain compulsory. — It restates an opinion after reasons; the others are a description, an event and a fact.","h":"تعيد الرأي بعد الأسباب."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Al-Masmak Fortress is an important historic building in Riyadh. (2) It was built of clay and mud bricks in the nineteenth century. (3) In 1902, King Abdulaziz captured it, which was the start of the unification of Saudi Arabia. (4) Today, it is a museum that tells the story of that event. (5) Riyadh also has many modern shopping malls. (6) Thousands of students visit it every year to learn about their history."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 5 — Modern shopping malls are off the topic of the historic fortress.","h":"المراكز التجارية خارج موضوع القصر التاريخي."},{"n":22,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","For example","However","Similarly"],"x":["The hotel was expensive. ______, the service was excellent, so we did not regret staying there."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] However — expensive / excellent service is a contrast.","h":"التضاد يحتاج However."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4","2 – 3 – 1 – 4","1 – 2 – 3 – 4","2 – 1 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) When we arrived, the waves were too high for swimming.","(2) Last Friday, we drove to the beach in Al-Khobar.","(3) Instead, we built sandcastles and played football on the sand.","(4) It turned out to be one of our best days out."],"k":0,"e":"[best order] 2 – 1 – 3 – 4 — trip → problem → Instead → result.","h":"رحلة ثم مشكلة ثم بديل ثم نتيجة."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Books were cheaper in the past.","Some people prefer watching television.","So he borrowed books from the mosque library and read every evening.","Libraries close at nine o'clock."],"x":["My father always says that reading is the best investment. When he was young, his family could not afford many books. ______ Today, he has a library of more than a thousand books at home."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph] So he borrowed books from the mosque library and read every evening. — The gap shows how he solved the problem and kept reading.","h":"الجملة تبين كيف حل المشكلة."},{"n":25,"s":"One of my cousins (A) live in (B) London, and (C) he (D) studies engineering there.","o":["live","London","he","studies"],"k":0,"e":"[error] live — The subject is One (singular): lives.","h":"الفاعل One مفرد."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence is the most suitable for a formal descriptive essay?","o":["The fortress was put up ages ago.","The fortress was constructed in the nineteenth century.","They built the fortress, like, a long time back.","The fortress is super old."],"k":1,"e":"[word choice / register] The fortress was constructed in the nineteenth century. — Formal vocabulary (constructed) and a precise time.","h":"مفردات رسمية وزمن دقيق."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Bird migration is one of nature's most amazing journeys.","Europe is colder than Africa in winter.","Saudi Arabia has many kinds of birds.","The Earth's magnetic field protects us from the sun."],"x":["______ Some fly thousands of kilometres from Europe to Africa every autumn. They use the sun, the stars and the Earth's magnetic field to find their way. Many stop in Saudi Arabia to rest and feed."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] Bird migration is one of nature's most amazing journeys. — The details describe bird migration.","h":"التفاصيل عن هجرة الطيور."},{"n":28,"s":"Which is written correctly?","o":["The guide whose family has lived in AlUla for generations. He knew every rock and tomb.","The guide, whose family has lived in AlUla for generations, knew every rock and tomb.","The guide, who his family has lived in AlUla for generations, knew every rock and tomb.","The guide, whose family has lived in AlUla for generations knew, every rock and tomb."],"k":1,"e":"[error] The guide, whose family has lived in AlUla for generations, knew every rock and tomb. — whose shows possession, and the clause sits between commas.","h":"whose للملكية بين فاصلتين."},{"n":29,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["because","therefore","whereas","so that"],"x":["Jeddah is humid and close to the sea, ______ Riyadh is dry and far from the coast."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] whereas — whereas compares two opposite facts.","h":"whereas للمقارنة."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Learning to swim was one of the best decisions I have made. (2) Swimming pools use a lot of chlorine. (3) At first, I was afraid of the water. (4) My coach taught me to breathe calmly and float. (5) After three months, I could swim fifty metres without stopping. (6) Now I swim twice a week and feel healthier than ever. (7) I hope to join the school team next year."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 2 — Chlorine in pools is not part of the writer's story.","h":"الكلور خارج قصة الكاتب."}]}],"n":30},{"id":"3.6","t":"Editing: Agreement, Tense Consistency, Pronoun Reference","html":"<p><strong>Unit 3 · Lesson 3.6 · CEFR B1 · STEP link: Composition Analysis (10%)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Find and correct errors in subject–verb agreement, tense consistency and pronoun reference.</p>\n<p>2. Edit a paragraph before handing it in.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكتشف الطالب أخطاء التطابق بين الفاعل والفعل وثبات الزمن ومرجع الضمير ويصححها.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يراجع الفقرة ويصححها قبل تسليمها.</span></p>\n<h3>The Skill</h3>\n<p>SUBJECT–VERB AGREEMENT: the verb must agree with the real subject, not with the noun nearest to it. 'The list of items IS on the table' (the subject is list). Watch out for: a lot of + plural (a lot of people ARE), the number of + singular (the number IS), each / every / everyone / neither of + singular, the news / mathematics + singular, and neither … nor or either … or, where the verb agrees with the NEARER subject (Neither my parents nor my brother WAS at home).</p>\n<p>TENSE CONSISTENCY: do not change tense without a reason. If a story is in the past, all the events stay in the past: 'Yesterday, my father went to the market and BOUGHT vegetables' (not buys). Change tense only when the time really changes: 'My grandparents lived in a village when they were young, but now they LIVE in Riyadh.' Also remember for + a period and since + a point in time.</p>\n<p>PRONOUN REFERENCE: every pronoun must clearly match the noun it refers to in number and person. 'The teacher gave the students their papers and told THEM to start' (not him). 'The museum is popular because IT has many exhibits' (not they). Use subject pronouns as subjects (My sister and I went …) and object pronouns as objects (… with my sister and me). Do not switch between you and one in the same sentence. In STEP, error items in paragraphs often test exactly these three areas.</p>\n<p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>agreement</strong> The list of items are on the table. → The list of items is on the table.</p>\n<p><strong>agreement</strong> There is a lot of people outside. → There are a lot of people outside.</p>\n<p><strong>neither … nor</strong> Neither my parents nor my brother were at home. → … nor my brother was at home.</p>\n<p><strong>tense</strong> Yesterday, he went to the market and buys vegetables. → … and bought vegetables.</p>\n<p><strong>tense change OK</strong> They lived in a village when they were young, but now they live in Riyadh.</p>\n<p><strong>pronoun</strong> The teacher gave the students their papers and told him to start. → … told them to start.</p>\n<p><strong>pronoun case</strong> My sister and me went to the fair. → My sister and I went to the fair.</p>\n<p><strong>for / since</strong> He has worked there since three years. → He has worked there for three years.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المهارة</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">التطابق: يتطابق الفعل مع الفاعل الحقيقي لا مع أقرب اسم إليه، فنقول The list of items is، وa lot of people are، وThe number is، وeach وeveryone مفرد، وفي neither … nor يطابق الفعل الفاعل الأقرب. ثبات الزمن: لا تغيّر الزمن دون سبب، فالقصة الماضية تبقى في الماضي. مرجع الضمير: يجب أن يطابق الضمير الاسم الذي يعود إليه في العدد والشخص، ونستخدم I فاعلًا وme مفعولًا، ولا ننتقل بين you وone.</span></p>\n<h3>Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. For each verb, find its real subject (ignore phrases like of items, of the survey).</p>\n<p>2. Check singular subjects: each, every, everyone, the number of, the news, mathematics, one of.</p>\n<p>3. Find the time of the paragraph (Yesterday, Every day, Now) and check that all verbs match it.</p>\n<p>4. For each pronoun, find the noun it refers to and check number (it / they) and case (I / me).</p>\n<p>5. Read the edited sentence aloud to check that it sounds natural.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الفاعل الحقيقي لكل فعل، وتحقق من الفاعلات المفردة، وحدد زمن الفقرة وطابق الأفعال معه، وابحث عن مرجع كل ضمير وتحقق من العدد والحالة، ثم اقرأ الجملة المصححة بصوت عالٍ.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Traps and Common Mistakes</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>✗ A verb that agrees with the nearest noun instead of the real subject.</p>\n<p>✗ A present verb in the middle of a past-tense story.</p>\n<p>✗ they or them referring to a singular noun (the museum, the company).</p>\n<p>✗ me used as a subject (My friend and me went …).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The box of old photographs (A) <u>were</u> (B) <u>found</u> in (C) <u>my grandmother's</u> (D) <u>cupboard</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. were B. found</p>\n<p>C. my grandmother's D. cupboard</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> Find the real subject: The box (of old photographs is a description).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> box is singular, so the verb must be singular.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is A: was.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: A</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">تجاهل of old photographs وابحث عن الفاعل الحقيقي.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. Last week, I (A) <u>went</u> to the library and (B) <u>borrow</u> three (C) <u>books</u> (D) <u>about</u> space.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. went B. borrow C. books D. about</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The time is Last week, and the first verb is went (past).</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The second action happened at the same time, so it must also be past.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is B: borrowed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: B</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حافظ على الزمن نفسه في القصة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. When the students finished (A) <u>their</u> tests, the teacher (B) <u>collected</u> (C) <u>it</u> and (D) <u>thanked</u> them.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. their B. collected C. it D. thanked</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> What did the teacher collect? The tests.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> tests is plural, so the pronoun must be them.</p>\n<p><strong>Think:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Answer: C</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ابحث عن الاسم الذي يعود إليه الضمير وتحقق من العدد.</span></p>\n<h3>Writing Task W-B1-06 — A volunteering experience (write, then edit)</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Task:</strong> Write 100–150 words about a volunteering experience (real or imagined). Then edit your paragraph: check every verb for agreement and tense, and every pronoun for reference.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتب من مئة إلى مئة وخمسين كلمة عن تجربة تطوع (حقيقية أو متخيلة)، ثم راجع فقرتك: تحقق من تطابق كل فعل وزمنه، ومن مرجع كل ضمير.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Planning frame</strong></p>\n<p>1. Topic sentence: when, where and what kind of volunteering.</p>\n<p>2. What you did every day.</p>\n<p>3. A difficulty you faced at first.</p>\n<p>4. How you overcame it.</p>\n<p>5. A special person or moment.</p>\n<p>6. What you learned, and your plans for the future.</p>\n<p><strong>Model answer (113 words; target 100–150)</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Last summer, I volunteered at a centre for children with special needs in Riyadh. Every morning, I helped the teachers prepare activities, and in the afternoon I played games with the children. At first, I was nervous because I did not know how to communicate with them. However, the staff gave me useful advice, and I soon became more confident. One boy, Fahad, could not speak, but he loved drawing. Every day, he drew a picture for me, and by the end of the summer I had a whole collection. This experience taught me patience and showed me that every child has a special talent. I hope to volunteer there again next year.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Examiner's commentary</strong></p>\n<p>▸ All the past events stay in the past tense (volunteered, helped, gave, drew).</p>\n<p>▸ The tense changes only for a general truth (every child has) and a future plan (I hope).</p>\n<p>▸ Every pronoun is clear: them = the children, he = Fahad.</p>\n<p>▸ Singular subjects take singular verbs: the staff gave, every child has.</p>\n<p><strong>Self-check before you hand in</strong></p>\n<p>☐ Does every verb agree with its real subject?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I keep the same tense for the events of my story?</p>\n<p>☐ Does every pronoun clearly refer to one noun with the same number?</p>\n<p>☐ Did I use I as a subject and me as an object?</p>\n<p>☐ Is my paragraph 100–150 words?</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد الكتابة راجع كل فعل وكل ضمير، وتأكد من ثبات زمن القصة.</span></p>","wu":"Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Read each paragraph or sentence carefully and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها. اقرأ كل فقرة أو جملة بعناية واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Lesson Focus (Questions 1–20)","الجزء الأول: أسئلة على مهارة الدرس."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"The list of items (A) are on (B) the table (C) next to (D) the door.","o":["are","the","next to","the door"],"k":0,"e":"[error] are — The subject is list (singular): is.","h":"الفاعل list مفرد."},{"n":2,"s":"Yesterday, my father (A) went to the market and (B) buys some (C) fresh (D) vegetables.","o":["went","buys","fresh","vegetables"],"k":1,"e":"[error] buys — The story is in the past: bought.","h":"الزمن ماضٍ: bought."},{"n":3,"s":"Every student (A) must bring (B) their own (C) lunch, because the canteen (D) are closed today.","o":["must","their","lunch","are"],"k":3,"e":"[error] are — the canteen is singular: is.","h":"the canteen مفرد."},{"n":4,"s":"(A) Last week, my sister (B) and (C) me (D) went to the book fair.","o":["Last week","and","me","went"],"k":2,"e":"[error] me — The subject needs the subject pronoun: My sister and I.","h":"الفاعل يحتاج I."},{"n":5,"s":"When I (A) opened the door, I (B) see a large box (C) on (D) the floor.","o":["opened","see","on","the"],"k":1,"e":"[error] see — Both actions are in the past: saw.","h":"الحدثان في الماضي: saw."},{"n":6,"s":"The teacher gave the students (A) their exam papers, and (B) she (C) told (D) him to start.","o":["their","she","told","him"],"k":3,"e":"[error] him — him should refer to the students (plural): them.","h":"الضمير يعود إلى الطلاب: them."},{"n":7,"s":"There (A) is a lot of (B) people (C) waiting (D) outside the stadium.","o":["is","people","waiting","outside"],"k":0,"e":"[error] is — a lot of people is plural: There are.","h":"الجمع يحتاج there are."},{"n":8,"s":"My favourite subject (A) is mathematics because the problems (B) is challenging and (C) fun to (D) solve.","o":["is","is","fun","solve"],"k":1,"e":"[error] is — the problems is plural: are.","h":"the problems جمع: are."},{"n":9,"s":"Which sentence keeps the tense consistent?","o":["Last year, we visited Abha and stayed in a small hotel.","Last year, we visit Abha and stayed in a small hotel.","Last year, we visited Abha and stay in a small hotel.","Last year, we have visited Abha and stayed in a small hotel."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Last year, we visited Abha and stayed in a small hotel. — Both verbs are in the past simple.","h":"الفعلان في الماضي البسيط."},{"n":10,"s":"My brother (A) has (B) been working in Dubai (C) since three years, and he (D) loves his job.","o":["has","been","since","loves"],"k":2,"e":"[error] since — A period of time needs for: for three years.","h":"المدة تحتاج for."},{"n":11,"s":"The company (A) announced that (B) its profits (C) has (D) increased this year.","o":["announced","its","has","increased"],"k":2,"e":"[error] has — profits is plural: have increased.","h":"profits جمع: have."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence uses pronouns correctly?","o":["The children finished his homework before they went out.","The children finished their homework before he went out.","The children finished they homework before they went out.","The children finished their homework before they went out."],"k":3,"e":"[error] The children finished their homework before they went out. — their and they both refer to the children (plural).","h":"their وthey تعودان إلى الأطفال."},{"n":13,"s":"Neither my parents nor my (A) brother (B) were at home (C) when the parcel (D) arrived.","o":["brother","were","when","arrived"],"k":1,"e":"[error] were — With neither … nor, the verb agrees with the nearer subject (my brother): was.","h":"الفعل يطابق الفاعل الأقرب."},{"n":14,"s":"Everyone (A) was talking about the news because (B) it (C) were so (D) shocking.","o":["was","it","were","shocking"],"k":2,"e":"[error] were — it (the news) is singular: was.","h":"it مفرد: was."},{"n":15,"s":"Which paragraph is edited correctly?","o":["Last week, our class goes to a farm. We fed the animals and picked some vegetables.","Last week, our class went to a farm. We fed the animals and picked some vegetables.","Last week, our class went to a farm. We feed the animals and picked some vegetables.","Last week, our class went to a farm. We fed the animals and pick some vegetables."],"k":1,"e":"[error] Last week, our class went to a farm. We fed the animals and picked some vegetables. — All the verbs are in the past.","h":"كل الأفعال في الماضي."},{"n":16,"s":"If you (A) want to improve your English, (B) one (C) should read every day and (D) you should practise speaking.","o":["want","one","should","you"],"k":1,"e":"[error] one — Do not switch from you to one in the same sentence: you should.","h":"لا تنتقل من you إلى one."},{"n":17,"s":"The museum is very popular because (A) it (B) has many (C) interesting exhibits, and (D) they attracts thousands of visitors every year.","o":["it","has","interesting","they"],"k":3,"e":"[error] they — The museum is singular: it attracts.","h":"the museum مفرد: it."},{"n":18,"s":"My grandparents (A) lived in a small village when they (B) were young, but now they (C) lived in (D) Riyadh.","o":["lived","were","lived","Riyadh"],"k":2,"e":"[error] lived — now needs the present: live.","h":"now تحتاج المضارع."},{"n":19,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["Both of my sisters is studying medicine.","Both of my sister are studying medicine.","Both my sisters studies medicine.","Both of my sisters are studying medicine."],"k":3,"e":"[error] Both of my sisters are studying medicine. — Both of + plural noun + plural verb.","h":"Both of مع جمع وفعل جمع."},{"n":20,"s":"The results of the survey (A) shows that most (B) students (C) prefer to study (D) in the morning.","o":["shows","students","prefer","in the morning"],"k":0,"e":"[error] shows — The subject is results (plural): show.","h":"الفاعل results جمع."}]},{"l":["Part B — Mixed STEP Composition Analysis (Questions 21–30)","الجزء الثاني: أسئلة متنوعة من قسم تحليل الكتابة في اختبار STEP."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Volunteering at the food bank taught me a lot. (2) I learned how to organize donations. (3) I met people from many different backgrounds. (4) Food prices have risen sharply this year. (5) Most importantly, I learned how lucky I am. (6) I plan to volunteer again next summer."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence] Sentence 4 — Rising food prices are not something the writer learned from volunteering.","h":"ارتفاع الأسعار ليس مما تعلمه الكاتب."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["There are many ways for young people to serve their community.","Beaches are often dirty after holidays.","Elderly people need regular exercise.","Some children stay in hospital for weeks."],"x":["______ Volunteers clean beaches, plant trees and collect rubbish from parks. Others help elderly people with their shopping or visit children in hospital."],"k":0,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis] There are many ways for young people to serve their community. — The details are different kinds of community service.","h":"التفاصيل أنواع من خدمة المجتمع."},{"n":23,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Therefore","For instance","Nevertheless","In addition"],"x":["She had never done any volunteering before. ______, she quickly became one of the most active members of the team."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector] Nevertheless — no experience / most active is a surprising contrast.","h":"تضاد مفاجئ."},{"n":24,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) After the training, we were divided into teams of four.","(2) Last summer, I joined a volunteer programme at the National Museum.","(3) Each team was responsible for guiding visitors in one gallery.","(4) On the first day, we attended a training session about the museum's history."],"k":3,"e":"[best order] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — joined → first day training → After the training, teams → each team's job.","h":"ترتيب زمني."},{"n":25,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Communication is important in every job.","In short, volunteering benefits everyone involved.","Some volunteers work every weekend.","Making friends can be difficult."],"x":["Volunteering is good for the community, but it is also good for the volunteers themselves. They develop skills such as communication and leadership. They meet new people and make friends. Many also say that helping others makes them feel happier. ______"],"k":1,"e":"[concluding sentence] In short, volunteering benefits everyone involved. — The conclusion sums up the benefits for both sides.","h":"الخاتمة تلخص الفوائد للطرفين."},{"n":26,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["We worked for six hours and filled more than a hundred bags with rubbish.","Plastic takes hundreds of years to break down.","Jeddah is a large city on the Red Sea.","Some beaches are cleaned by the municipality."],"x":["Our team was asked to clean a beach near Jeddah. When we arrived, we were shocked by the amount of plastic on the sand. ______ By the end of the day, the beach looked completely different."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph] We worked for six hours and filled more than a hundred bags with rubbish. — The gap describes the work that changed the beach.","h":"الجملة تصف العمل الذي غيّر الشاطئ."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence is the most appropriate for a formal report about a volunteering project?","o":["The project was completed successfully within the planned time.","We totally nailed the project on time.","The project went pretty awesome.","Everything was cool with the project."],"k":0,"e":"[word choice / register] The project was completed successfully within the planned time. — A formal report needs neutral, formal language.","h":"التقرير الرسمي بلغة رسمية."},{"n":28,"s":"The volunteers (A) who (B) works at the shelter (C) are all (D) university students.","o":["who","works","are","university"],"k":1,"e":"[error] works — who refers to the volunteers (plural): work.","h":"who تعود إلى جمع: work."},{"n":29,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["so","because","for example","but"],"x":["Many people want to volunteer, ______ they do not know where to start."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector] but — want to / do not know how is a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج but."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence keeps the tense consistent?","o":["Every Saturday, she visits the hospital and reads stories to the children.","Every Saturday, she visits the hospital and read stories to the children.","Every Saturday, she visited the hospital and reads stories to the children.","Every Saturday, she visits the hospital and reading stories to the children."],"k":0,"e":"[error] Every Saturday, she visits the hospital and reads stories to the children. — A routine uses the present simple for both verbs.","h":"العادة بالمضارع البسيط."}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions covering all six lessons of the unit. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا تغطي دروس الوحدة الستة، اختر الإجابة الصحيحة."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["However","For instance","Moreover","Therefore"],"x":["The road was wet. ______, the driver slowed down."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] Therefore — Slowing down is the result of the wet road.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج Therefore."},{"n":2,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) The Saudi national day is celebrated on 23 September. (2) Streets and buildings are decorated with green flags. (3) Green tea is popular in many Asian countries. (4) Families watch fireworks and air shows. (5) Many people wear traditional clothes. (6) It is a day of national pride and unity."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 3 — Green tea shares the word green but is off the topic.","h":"الشاي الأخضر يشترك في الكلمة فقط."},{"n":3,"s":"My cousin (A) and his friends (B) is (C) planning a trip (D) to Abha.","o":["and","is","planning","to"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 3.6] is — My cousin and his friends is plural: are.","h":"فاعل جمع: are."},{"n":4,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Schools in Saudi Arabia have long summer holidays.","Breakfast is the most important meal of the day.","This is usually because they go to bed very late.","Some students live near their schools."],"x":["Many students find it hard to wake up early for school. ______ As a result, they often miss breakfast and arrive tired."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] This is usually because they go to bed very late. — The gap explains the cause of the problem, which leads to the result.","h":"الجملة تشرح سبب المشكلة."},{"n":5,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 3","2 – 1 – 3 – 4"],"x":["(1) Then she trained as a teacher at King Saud University.","(2) My aunt Latifa always dreamed of becoming a teacher.","(3) Today, she is the head teacher of a large girls' school.","(4) After graduating, she taught Arabic for fifteen years."],"k":0,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 1 – 4 – 3 — dream → training → teaching → today.","h":"ترتيب زمني."},{"n":6,"s":"Which sentence would make the best topic sentence for a NARRATIVE paragraph?","o":["Storms are common in the north of the country in winter.","Electricity is produced in large power stations.","The night the power went out during the storm, our family discovered how much we depend on electricity.","I believe every home should have a generator."],"k":2,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 3.5] The night the power went out during the storm, our family discovered how much we depend on electricity. — It introduces an event to be told as a story.","h":"تقدم حدثًا يُروى."},{"n":7,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["As a result","For example","On the other hand","Furthermore"],"x":["Some people enjoy living in busy cities. ______, others prefer the peace and quiet of the countryside."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] On the other hand — Two opposite preferences.","h":"تفضيلان متعاكسان."},{"n":8,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Many young Saudis are choosing careers in technology. (2) Universities now offer more programmes in computer science and engineering. (3) Big companies are opening offices in Riyadh and Jeddah. (4) Salaries in the technology sector are often high. (5) Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia. (6) Online courses also make it easier to learn programming. (7) Technology is likely to remain a popular career choice for years to come."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 5 — The size of Riyadh does not explain career choices in technology.","h":"حجم الرياض لا يفسر اختيار التقنية."},{"n":9,"s":"The number of tourists (A) visiting AlUla (B) have (C) grown rapidly (D) in recent years.","o":["visiting","have","grown","in recent years"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 3.6] have — The number is singular: has grown.","h":"The number مفرد."},{"n":10,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["This often meant waiting in long queues for an hour or more.","Banks were usually closed on Fridays.","Mobile phones were very expensive at first.","Money is still printed on paper."],"x":["In the past, people had to visit a bank to transfer money. ______ Today, most transfers are done in seconds using a mobile phone."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] This often meant waiting in long queues for an hour or more. — The gap describes the difficulty of the past, contrasted with today.","h":"الجملة تصف صعوبة الماضي."},{"n":11,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3","2 – 1 – 4 – 5 – 3","1 – 2 – 4 – 5 – 3","2 – 1 – 5 – 4 – 3"],"x":["(1) First, the old building was carefully cleaned.","(2) The city decided to turn an old factory into a public library.","(3) Finally, the library opened to the public last month.","(4) Next, architects designed modern reading rooms inside it.","(5) Then thousands of books were donated by local families."],"k":1,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 1 – 4 – 5 – 3 — decision → First → Next → Then → Finally.","h":"قرار ثم خطوات."},{"n":12,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Every corner of the house seems to hold a memory of the past.","Hail is famous for its mountains.","Mud houses are cheaper than modern ones.","My grandfather was a farmer."],"x":["My grandfather's old house in Hail has thick mud walls and a large wooden door. Inside, the rooms are cool even in summer. In the courtyard, there is an old well and a palm tree. The smell of cardamom coffee always fills the main room. ______"],"k":0,"e":"[concluding sentence · 3.5] Every corner of the house seems to hold a memory of the past. — The description ends with an overall impression.","h":"الوصف ينتهي بانطباع عام."},{"n":13,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Even though","Because","Since","As a result"],"x":["______ he had studied very hard, he did not pass the driving test."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] Even though — Studying hard / not passing is a contrast inside one sentence.","h":"تضاد داخل جملة واحدة."},{"n":14,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) A healthy diet includes a variety of foods. (2) Fast-food restaurants are open late at night. (3) Fruit and vegetables provide vitamins and fibre. (4) Fish, eggs and beans are good sources of protein. (5) Whole grains give the body energy. (6) Eating a variety of foods keeps the body strong and healthy."],"k":1,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 2 — Restaurant opening hours do not describe a healthy diet.","h":"مواعيد المطاعم خارج الموضوع."},{"n":15,"s":"Which sentence uses pronouns correctly?","o":["The company thanked their workers for its hard work.","The company thanked it's workers for their hard work.","The company thanked its workers for their hard work.","The company thanked its workers for they hard work."],"k":2,"e":"[error · 3.6] The company thanked its workers for their hard work. — its = the company's; their = the workers'.","h":"its للشركة وtheir للعمال."},{"n":16,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["These plants will provide electricity for millions of homes without polluting the air.","The desert is very hot during the day.","Oil is still the country's main export.","Some houses have solar panels on their roofs."],"x":["Saudi Arabia is building huge solar power plants in the desert. ______ In the future, the country hopes to export clean energy to other countries."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] These plants will provide electricity for millions of homes without polluting the air. — The gap explains the benefit of the plants before the future plan.","h":"الجملة تشرح فائدة المحطات."},{"n":17,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","4 – 2 – 3 – 1","2 – 4 – 1 – 3"],"x":["(1) As a result, the number of visitors doubled in one year.","(2) The old museum had very few visitors.","(3) To change this, the managers added interactive screens and activities for children.","(4) Its exhibits were old, and there was nothing for young people to do."],"k":1,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 4 – 3 – 1 — problem → reason → solution → result.","h":"مشكلة ثم سبب ثم حل ثم نتيجة."},{"n":18,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["New restaurants open every month in our city.","Waiters should be trained carefully.","The restaurant is near the shopping mall.","Our dinner at the new restaurant was a complete disappointment."],"x":["______ The waiter forgot our order twice, and the food arrived cold. When we complained, the manager was rude to us. We left without finishing our meal."],"k":3,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 3.5] Our dinner at the new restaurant was a complete disappointment. — The narrative needs an opening that introduces the event and its meaning.","h":"افتتاح السرد يقدم الحدث."},{"n":19,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Nevertheless","For instance","In contrast","Consequently"],"x":["Water is scarce in Saudi Arabia. ______, people should use it carefully."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] Consequently — Careful use is the result of scarcity.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج Consequently."},{"n":20,"s":"Last Ramadan, my family (A) visited Makkah, and we (B) pray in the (C) Grand Mosque (D) every night.","o":["visited","pray","Grand","every"],"k":1,"e":"[error · 3.6] pray — The story is in the past: prayed.","h":"الزمن ماضٍ: prayed."},{"n":21,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) The Empty Quarter is one of the largest sand deserts in the world. (2) It covers parts of Saudi Arabia, Oman, the UAE and Yemen. (3) Some of its sand dunes are more than two hundred metres high. (4) Many deserts are cold at night in winter. (5) Very few people live there because of the extreme heat. (6) Scientists have found evidence that it was once covered by lakes. (7) Today, it attracts adventurous tourists from around the world."],"k":0,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 4 — A general fact about many deserts is not about the Empty Quarter.","h":"حقيقة عامة لا تخص الربع الخالي."},{"n":22,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Mobile phones have many useful apps.","Some teachers use phones to take photos.","However, after a few weeks, they noticed that they could concentrate much better in class.","Lessons at our school last forty-five minutes."],"x":["Our school recently banned mobile phones during lessons. At first, many students complained. ______ Most students now agree that the rule was a good idea."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] However, after a few weeks, they noticed that they could concentrate much better in class. — The gap explains why students changed their minds.","h":"الجملة تشرح تغير رأي الطلاب."},{"n":23,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 4 – 3","4 – 2 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 3 – 1"],"x":["(1) For example, Saudi coffee is served with dates to every guest.","(2) Hospitality is an important value in Saudi culture.","(3) Guests are always offered the best seat in the house.","(4) It is shown in many small customs."],"k":2,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 4 – 1 – 3 — general value → small customs → For example → another custom.","h":"من العام إلى الأمثلة."},{"n":24,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Many famous chefs started cooking at a young age.","Healthy food can be expensive in some shops.","Some students already help their parents in the kitchen.","For all these reasons, cooking classes should be part of the school curriculum."],"x":["In my opinion, every student should learn to cook before finishing school. Cooking is a basic life skill that everyone needs. It also helps people eat more healthily and spend less money. Moreover, it can be a creative and relaxing hobby. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence · 3.5] For all these reasons, cooking classes should be part of the school curriculum. — The opinion is restated as a recommendation.","h":"إعادة الرأي توصيةً."},{"n":25,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Similarly","In contrast","As a result","For instance"],"x":["The first part of the book was slow and boring. ______, the second part was full of action."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] In contrast — slow / full of action is a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج In contrast."},{"n":26,"s":"Each of the students (A) were (B) given a certificate (C) at the end of (D) the course.","o":["were","given","at","the"],"k":0,"e":"[error · 3.6] were — Each is singular: was given.","h":"Each مفرد."},{"n":27,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6"],"x":["(1) The first car I remember was my father's old pickup truck. (2) It was white, with a long scratch on the door. (3) We drove it to the desert every winter. (4) Once, it got stuck in the sand for three hours. (5) My father still talks about it with a smile. (6) Pickup trucks are very popular in the Gulf region."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 6 — A general fact about pickup trucks is not part of the writer's memory.","h":"حقيقة عامة خارج ذكرى الكاتب."},{"n":28,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Most tools are designed for right-handed people.","Writing with the left hand can be difficult.","In fact, about one in ten people in the world is left-handed.","Some people can use both hands equally well."],"x":["Many people believe that left-handed people are rare. ______ Famous left-handed people include artists, scientists and sports champions."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] In fact, about one in ten people in the world is left-handed. — The gap corrects the belief before the examples.","h":"الجملة تصحح الاعتقاد."},{"n":29,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) Luckily, a police officer saw what happened and stopped him.","(2) Last week, my uncle's car broke down on a busy road.","(3) He got out to check the engine.","(4) Suddenly, another driver almost hit him."],"k":2,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 3 – 4 – 1 — breakdown → got out → Suddenly → Luckily.","h":"ترتيب أحداث القصة."},{"n":30,"s":"Which sentence would make the best topic sentence for an OPINION paragraph?","o":["Our school starts at seven o'clock.","I strongly believe that schools should start later in the morning.","Yesterday, I was late for school because of traffic.","The school building has three floors."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 3.5] I strongly believe that schools should start later in the morning. — It states an opinion that reasons can support.","h":"تذكر رأيًا."},{"n":31,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["However","Otherwise","In fact","On the other hand"],"x":["My brother is very talented at drawing. ______, he won first prize in a national art competition last year."],"k":2,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] In fact — In fact adds strong evidence for the first statement.","h":"In fact تضيف دليلًا قويًا."},{"n":32,"s":"Which paragraph is edited correctly?","o":["Every morning, my mother wakes up at five. She prays and then prepares breakfast for the family.","Every morning, my mother wakes up at five. She prayed and then prepares breakfast for the family.","Every morning, my mother wake up at five. She prays and then prepares breakfast for the family.","Every morning, my mother wakes up at five. They pray and then prepares breakfast for the family."],"k":0,"e":"[error · 3.6] Every morning, my mother wakes up at five. She prays and then prepares breakfast for the family. — Present simple throughout, singular verbs and a correct pronoun.","h":"مضارع بسيط وأفعال مفردة وضمير صحيح."},{"n":33,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["The moon is closer to the Earth than the sun.","Ramadan is a month of fasting.","As a result, a Hijri year is shorter than a year in the solar calendar.","Many countries use the solar calendar for business."],"x":["The Hijri calendar is based on the movements of the moon. ______ This is why Ramadan comes about eleven days earlier each year."],"k":2,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] As a result, a Hijri year is shorter than a year in the solar calendar. — 'This is why' needs the fact that explains the earlier date.","h":"This is why تحتاج السبب."},{"n":34,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) My best friend Rakan is very generous. (2) He always shares his lunch with students who forget theirs. (3) Last year, he gave half of his savings to a charity. (4) He is also the tallest student in our class. (5) Everyone respects him for his kindness."],"k":2,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 4 — His height does not show generosity.","h":"طوله لا يدل على كرمه."},{"n":35,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 5 – 4 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 5 – 1 – 3","4 – 2 – 5 – 1 – 3","2 – 4 – 1 – 5 – 3"],"x":["(1) After that, the dates are sorted by size and quality.","(2) Dates are harvested in late summer.","(3) Finally, they are packed in boxes and sent to markets.","(4) First, farmers climb the palm trees and cut down the bunches.","(5) Then the dates are washed and dried."],"k":1,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 4 – 5 – 1 – 3 — topic → First → Then → After that → Finally.","h":"مراحل حصاد التمر."},{"n":36,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Swimming races are usually held in summer.","My father was a good swimmer when he was young.","Some swimmers train for many hours every day.","That day, I learned that finishing what you start matters more than winning."],"x":["When I was eight, I entered a swimming race for the first time. I was the youngest swimmer, and the others looked much stronger. Halfway through the race, I swallowed some water and almost stopped. But I heard my father shouting my name, so I kept going. I finished last, but I finished. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence · 3.5] That day, I learned that finishing what you start matters more than winning. — The narrative ends with the lesson learned.","h":"القصة تنتهي بالدرس المستفاد."},{"n":37,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["otherwise","therefore","moreover","for example"],"x":["You need to book your tickets early; ______, there may be no seats left."],"k":0,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] otherwise — otherwise = if you do not book early.","h":"otherwise بمعنى وإلا."},{"n":38,"s":"If a student (A) loses (B) his or her library card, (C) they (D) has to pay for a new one.","o":["loses","his","they","has"],"k":3,"e":"[error · 3.6] has — they takes a plural verb: have.","h":"they مع have."},{"n":39,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 4","Sentence 5","Sentence 6","Sentence 7"],"x":["(1) Learning to drive requires patience and practice. (2) New drivers must learn the rules of the road. (3) They need to practise parking and changing lanes. (4) A good instructor can help them feel confident. (5) Most driving schools offer both theory and practical lessons. (6) It usually takes several months to become a safe driver. (7) Some cars today can park themselves."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 7 — Self-parking cars are not about learning to drive.","h":"السيارات ذاتية الركن خارج الموضوع."},{"n":40,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Others, however, believe that homework helps children develop good study habits.","Primary school children usually finish school at noon.","Play is important for children's health.","Many parents help their children with homework."],"x":["Some experts say that homework should be banned in primary schools. They argue that young children need time to play and rest. ______ The best solution may be short, simple homework that takes no more than twenty minutes."],"k":0,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] Others, however, believe that homework helps children develop good study habits. — The gap gives the opposing view before the compromise.","h":"الجملة تقدم الرأي المقابل قبل الحل الوسط."},{"n":41,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 1 – 3 – 4 – 5","3 – 2 – 1 – 4 – 5","2 – 3 – 1 – 4 – 5","2 – 3 – 4 – 1 – 5"],"x":["(1) Second, it encourages them to exercise outdoors.","(2) Schools should create more green spaces.","(3) First, trees and plants make the air cleaner for students.","(4) Finally, green spaces can be used for science lessons about nature.","(5) For example, students could plant and care for their own vegetables."],"k":2,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 3 – 1 – 4 – 5 — opinion → First → Second → Finally → For example (of science lessons).","h":"رأي ثم أسباب ثم مثال."},{"n":42,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Fishing is an important industry in many countries.","The old fishing town is peaceful and beautiful in the evening.","Last year, we stayed in the town for a week.","I think the town should build more hotels."],"x":["______ At night, the narrow streets are lit by small lanterns, and the sound of the waves can be heard everywhere. The houses are white with blue doors, and flowers hang from every balcony."],"k":1,"e":"[topic sentence / thesis · 3.5] The old fishing town is peaceful and beautiful in the evening. — The descriptive details need an overall impression.","h":"الوصف يحتاج انطباعًا عامًا."},{"n":43,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Nevertheless","As a result","In contrast","Otherwise"],"x":["The new airport is larger and more modern than the old one. ______, it can handle twice as many passengers."],"k":1,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] As a result — More passengers is the result of the larger size.","h":"النتيجة تحتاج As a result."},{"n":44,"s":"The teacher, together with her students, (A) are (B) preparing (C) a (D) surprise for the principal.","o":["are","preparing","a","surprise"],"k":0,"e":"[error · 3.6] are — together with does not change the subject (The teacher): is.","h":"together with لا تغير الفاعل."},{"n":45,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Reading fiction can improve our ability to understand others. (2) When we read a story, we see the world through a character's eyes. (3) This helps us understand feelings that are different from our own. (4) Some novels have been made into successful films. (5) Studies show that regular readers of fiction are often more empathetic. (6) Fiction, therefore, is more than just entertainment."],"k":3,"e":"[irrelevant sentence · 3.1] Sentence 4 — Films made from novels do not support the idea of understanding others.","h":"الأفلام لا تدعم فكرة فهم الآخرين."},{"n":46,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Camel races have become a popular sport.","Its milk and meat were important sources of food.","Cars have replaced camels for most journeys.","Some camels are sold for very high prices."],"x":["The camel was essential to life in the Arabian desert for thousands of years. It carried people and goods across long distances. ______ Even its hair was woven into tents and clothes. It is no surprise that Arabic has hundreds of words for camels."],"k":1,"e":"[complete the paragraph · 3.4] Its milk and meat were important sources of food. — 'Even its hair' needs other uses of the camel before it.","h":"Even its hair تحتاج استخدامات أخرى قبلها."},{"n":47,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Tourists spend a lot of money on souvenirs.","Some villages are very difficult to reach.","Tourism is the largest industry in some countries.","Therefore, if it is managed well, tourism can help preserve culture rather than destroy it."],"x":["Some people believe that tourism damages traditional culture. It is true that large numbers of visitors can cause problems. However, tourism also creates jobs, and it encourages people to protect their heritage. In many villages, old crafts have been revived because tourists want to buy them. ______"],"k":3,"e":"[concluding sentence · 3.5] Therefore, if it is managed well, tourism can help preserve culture rather than destroy it. — The conclusion states the writer's balanced view.","h":"الخاتمة تذكر رأي الكاتب المتوازن."},{"n":48,"s":"Which sentence is correct?","o":["Neither of the answers is correct.","Neither of the answers are correct.","Neither of the answer are correct.","Neither the answers is correct."],"k":0,"e":"[error · 3.6] Neither of the answers is correct. — In formal writing, neither of takes a singular verb.","h":"neither of مع فعل مفرد في الكتابة الرسمية."},{"n":49,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 1 – 5 – 4","2 – 3 – 5 – 1 – 4","3 – 2 – 1 – 5 – 4","2 – 1 – 3 – 5 – 4"],"x":["(1) This means that one in three people will have to change their careers.","(2) Technology is changing the world of work faster than ever.","(3) Some experts predict that a third of today's jobs will disappear by 2040.","(4) Therefore, the most important skill for young people may be the ability to keep learning.","(5) At the same time, new jobs that we cannot imagine today will appear."],"k":0,"e":"[best order · 3.2] 2 – 3 – 1 – 5 – 4 — topic → prediction → This means → At the same time → Therefore.","h":"موضوع ثم توقع ثم نتيجته ثم الخلاصة."},{"n":50,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["Accordingly","For instance","Likewise","Nevertheless"],"x":["The plan to build a new shopping mall was popular with many residents. ______, environmental groups opposed it because it would destroy one of the city's last green areas."],"k":3,"e":"[transition / connector · 3.3] Nevertheless — popular / opposed is a contrast.","h":"تضاد يحتاج Nevertheless."}]}],"n":50}};
